1
00:00:00,167 --> 00:00:03,433
♪ In the
not-too-distant future ♪

2
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:06,733
♪ Next Sunday A.D. ♪

3
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:09,633
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

4
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:12,833
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

5
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:15,700
♪ He worked at
Gizmodic Institute ♪

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,133
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

7
00:00:19,133 --> 00:00:22,133
♪ He did a good job
cleaning up the place ♪

8
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:23,500
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,500
♪ So they shot him into space ♪
(engine roaring)

10
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,600
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,900
♪ The worst we can
find, la-la-la ♪

12
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,600
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

13
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,000
♪ And we'll monitor
his mind, la-la-la ♪

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,833
♪ Now keep in mind
Joel can't control ♪

15
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:47,033
♪ When the movies begin
or end, la-la-la ♪

16
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:50,100
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

17
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:53,633
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

18
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:56,800
♪ Robot roll-call ♪

19
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:58,100
♪ Cambot ♪
- Pan left.

20
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,567
♪ Gypsy ♪
- Hi, girls.

21
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:01,000
♪ Tom Servo ♪
- What a cool guy.

22
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,900
♪ Crow ♪
- I'm the wise-cracker.

23
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,633
♪ If you're wondering ♪
how he eats and breathes

24
00:01:05,633 --> 00:01:08,833
♪ And other science
facts, la-la-la ♪

25
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:10,133
♪ Then repeat to yourself ♪

26
00:01:10,133 --> 00:01:11,700
♪ It's just a show ♪

27
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,000
♪ I should really just relax ♪

28
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,833
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

29
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:21,600
(guitar strumming)

30
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,267
(doors closing)

31
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,433
- Hey everybody.

32
00:01:32,433 --> 00:01:33,667
My name's Joel.

33
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,000
Welcome to the
Satellite of Love.

34
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,333
- [Robots] Woah, movie
time, movie time!

35
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,633
(robots chuckle)

36
00:01:41,633 --> 00:01:42,467
- He did it!

37
00:01:42,467 --> 00:01:43,433
He actually did it!

38
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:44,867
- Hey, good one there, Cambot!

39
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:46,167
Boy, we really fazed him.
(Crow mumbles)

40
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:47,700
I didn't think he
was that gullible!

41
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:48,867
- Ah, what a maroon!
(Tom laughs)

42
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:50,767
- [Voiceover]
Control sign in five,

43
00:01:50,767 --> 00:01:54,167
four, three, two,
control sign out.

44
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:55,000
- Ah, hit the buzzer.

45
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,200
- I can't!

46
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,433
My arms are
inoperable, you do it.

47
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:58,733
- And my good ones
are in the shop, oh.

48
00:01:58,733 --> 00:01:59,967
(Crow grunts)

49
00:01:59,967 --> 00:02:03,467
(upbeat electronic music)

50
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:08,267
- Uh-oh, uh, it was
all in fun, Joel!

51
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:10,033
(robots chuckle)

52
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:11,133
- We were just
giving you the raz!

53
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:12,867
- (chuckles) Yeah.

54
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:15,433
- I'm just glad I programmed
you two knuckle-knobs

55
00:02:15,433 --> 00:02:17,967
to give me some occasional
good-natured ribbing.

56
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:19,833
(robots chuckle and sigh)

57
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:21,300
Ah, wait.

58
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,533
It looks like it's time
for the invention exchange.

59
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:24,000
(gas hissing)

60
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,067
- (gasps) Mommy, mommy!

61
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:27,067
Don't look at me!

62
00:02:27,067 --> 00:02:31,300
Don't ever look at me! (gasps)

63
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:34,000
- And don't drool this time!

64
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,367
Well, hello, booby.

65
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:36,900
This week's invention exchange

66
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:39,667
is an exciting foray into
the field of self-surgery,

67
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:42,133
much in keeping with the
theme of today's film.

68
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,833
All you need is a
willing subject,

69
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:45,433
a can of nitrous oxide

70
00:02:45,433 --> 00:02:48,400
and an oversized
version of the game

71
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,933
Operation.
(latch clicks)

72
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:52,600
Operation!

73
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:55,300
The goofy game
for dopey doctors!

74
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,500
Remove wrenched ankle.

75
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:00,867
- No, no!

76
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,833
Why, why?
(metal thunks)

77
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:06,300
Thank you.

78
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:07,667
- And it's all in the
name of science, you know?

79
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:09,667
But if you touch the sides...
(electricity buzzes)

80
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:13,000
(Frank screams)
(metal thunks)

81
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,233
- Thank you!

82
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:16,033
Well, you get the
idea, don't you?

83
00:03:16,033 --> 00:03:17,267
Don't you?

84
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:19,700
- [Tom] And you used to
work with these guys?

85
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,900
- Yeah, that's what I'm
talkin' about, you guys!

86
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,800
Again, me and the scientists
are in direct dichotomy.

87
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,233
They took Milton Bradley

88
00:03:26,233 --> 00:03:28,100
and turned him
into Doctor Phibes,

89
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:31,333
while I took this Day-Glo
x-ray fluoroscope,

90
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,167
chopped it, channeled it,

91
00:03:33,167 --> 00:03:34,567
added some thrush pipes,

92
00:03:34,567 --> 00:03:35,833
and came up with a game

93
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:38,067
that teaches you about
your body as you play!

94
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:39,167
- Hey, it's kinda like Twister!

95
00:03:39,167 --> 00:03:40,433
- Yeah!

96
00:03:40,433 --> 00:03:41,667
Everybody knows that
food in your throat

97
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:42,967
is called bolus.

98
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:45,267
I call this game pin-bolus!
(robots laugh)

99
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:46,533
Get it?

100
00:03:46,533 --> 00:03:48,133
Okay, as you can see, my
innards are all lit up.

101
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:49,367
(clears throat) I take this

102
00:03:49,367 --> 00:03:51,867
ordinary, Day-Glo barium

103
00:03:51,867 --> 00:03:53,133
meatball

104
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:54,933
and eat it. (gulps)

105
00:03:54,933 --> 00:03:55,767
(ball clatters and bells ring)

106
00:03:55,767 --> 00:03:56,767
- Wow!

107
00:03:56,767 --> 00:03:58,167
- Okay, then, as you can see,

108
00:03:58,167 --> 00:03:59,933
I can move my kidneys here,

109
00:03:59,933 --> 00:04:02,000
and it's kinda like
playing pinball!

110
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,433
(robots laugh)

111
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:04,800
- This gives a whole new meaning
to playing with your food,

112
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,967
doesn't it?
(Joel and Crow mutter)

113
00:04:05,967 --> 00:04:07,133
- Hey, if you score
enough points,

114
00:04:07,133 --> 00:04:08,433
do you get an extra
ball movement?

115
00:04:08,433 --> 00:04:11,600
(Crow cackles)
- [Tom] Aw, good one!

116
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,367
And, uh, does hopping around

117
00:04:14,367 --> 00:04:15,767
make it tilt or something?

118
00:04:15,767 --> 00:04:17,533
- No, but it will
make you throw up.

119
00:04:17,533 --> 00:04:18,567
- [Crow] Yeah.

120
00:04:18,567 --> 00:04:20,833
- And, (clears throat)

121
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:21,700
there's the pin-bolus!

122
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,500
(robots mutter)
Anyway,

123
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,000
what do you think, sirs?

124
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,867
- Oh, I'm feeling
much better now.

125
00:04:26,867 --> 00:04:28,100
Say,

126
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:29,300
could you give me
a glass of juice

127
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,767
with one of those little
bendy straws on it?

128
00:04:30,767 --> 00:04:32,133
I love those things.

129
00:04:32,133 --> 00:04:33,333
- Can it, Frank!
- [Frank] Just delightful.

130
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:35,933
(electricity buzzes
and Frank wails)

131
00:04:35,933 --> 00:04:37,333
Well, Joel,
(Frank whimpers)

132
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:38,567
today's film is a
plotless little peccadillo

133
00:04:38,567 --> 00:04:40,067
called Ring of Terror.

134
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:42,667
It's about some of the oldest
medical students in history.

135
00:04:42,667 --> 00:04:45,567
Chomp on it, but don't choke!

136
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:47,300
(alarms blare)
(Joel and robots scream)

137
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:49,233
(engines chug)

138
00:04:49,233 --> 00:04:50,300
(door clatters)

139
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,133
(door whooshes)

140
00:04:51,133 --> 00:04:51,967
(door thuds)

141
00:04:51,967 --> 00:04:53,000
(door chugs)

142
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,433
(door whirs)
(fire crackles)

143
00:04:54,433 --> 00:04:55,267
(door crashes)

144
00:04:55,267 --> 00:04:57,933
(ominous music)

145
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:00,500
- [Joel] Oh,

146
00:05:01,533 --> 00:05:02,733
what's that, Tom?

147
00:05:02,733 --> 00:05:03,667
It says--

148
00:05:03,667 --> 00:05:04,933
- [Tom and Joel] "Centerville,

149
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:09,133
"a real great place to
raise your kids up."

150
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:09,967
- [Tom] Hm.
- [Joel] Wow.

151
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:11,467
- [Tom] Neat.

152
00:05:11,467 --> 00:05:14,100
Hey, where do you suppose
those arrows are leading to?

153
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,633
- [Joel] Hm, I guess we'll fi--

154
00:05:15,633 --> 00:05:18,033
(dramatic music)
(Joel and robots scream)

155
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:19,967
- [Tom] Playstar Productions?

156
00:05:19,967 --> 00:05:21,300
I gotta look this one up.

157
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,133
Just a second, let's see.

158
00:05:22,133 --> 00:05:22,967
Um.

159
00:05:22,967 --> 00:05:24,067
Oh, here's the book.

160
00:05:24,067 --> 00:05:25,267
Uh, (stutters) Ring of Terror,

161
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:26,700
1962.

162
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:27,933
Bomb.

163
00:05:27,933 --> 00:05:29,300
Director Clark Paylow,

164
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,067
starring George
Mather, Esther Furst,

165
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:32,733
Austin Green, Joseph Conway.

166
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:34,233
"A medical student must confront

167
00:05:34,233 --> 00:05:36,533
"a corpse as a fraternity
initiation prank

168
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:38,800
"in this low-budget moo-zer."

169
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,833
Huh.
- [Crow] Hm.

170
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,033
- [Crow] Well, can we go then?

171
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:42,400
- [Tom] I think this
is the beginning

172
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,233
of a long, hard ride here.

173
00:05:45,233 --> 00:05:46,433
- [Joel] Oh, let's
go, uh, that way.

174
00:05:46,433 --> 00:05:47,600
- [Tom] No, wait!
- [Joel] Hey!

175
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:48,133
- [Tom] We're
supposed to go that

176
00:05:48,133 --> 00:05:48,800
way.

177
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,567
What gives?

178
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,867
Hm.

179
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:52,700
- [Joel] Hey,

180
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:54,167
hi, everybody.

181
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:55,100
(solemn march music)

182
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,833
Oh, I see.
(robots grumble)

183
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:59,433
- [Tom] Yeah, it's one of those.

184
00:06:01,267 --> 00:06:04,367
♪ Look for the Union radar ♪

185
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:07,000
♪ When you are dying and the ♪

186
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,433
- [Crow] Look, Lyndon
LaRouche's brother!

187
00:06:09,433 --> 00:06:11,067
They just bought drugs
from the Queen of England!

188
00:06:11,067 --> 00:06:12,300
- [Joel] Shoes by Botany 500,

189
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,533
body by Fischer.

190
00:06:13,533 --> 00:06:15,000
- [Crow] He looks
like Count Chocula.

191
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,433
- [Tom] Shouldn't they
have their high beams on?

192
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:18,500
- [Joel] It must be cold.

193
00:06:19,967 --> 00:06:20,933
- [Tom] Okay, everybody on set

194
00:06:20,933 --> 00:06:22,233
for the big Cossack number!

195
00:06:22,233 --> 00:06:23,700
- [Joel] Oh, the
caterers are here.

196
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,967
They must be serving
Tombstone pizza.

197
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:26,900
(Tom laughs)

198
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,400
- [Tom] Aw, look, she's mad

199
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:32,200
'cause she just lost her
job on Petticoat Junction.

200
00:06:33,567 --> 00:06:35,233
Ah, get that camera
outta my face!

201
00:06:35,233 --> 00:06:37,633
- [Joel] Ah, The
Funeral, by Henry Gibson.

202
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:39,167
- [Tom] Bocchia-cha-cha-chio,

203
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:42,600
that's my favorite Italian wine.

204
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,100
♪ Paylow, Palow ♪

205
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:47,233
♪ Director's gone and ♪
they want to go home ♪

206
00:06:47,233 --> 00:06:48,700
- [Tom] Yeah, I'm
the last guy in line.

207
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,100
And I like being there.

208
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,267
Go ahead and lay a,

209
00:06:52,267 --> 00:06:53,867
never mind.

210
00:06:53,867 --> 00:06:54,700
- [Joel] A graveyard?

211
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:55,967
What a coincidence?

212
00:06:55,967 --> 00:06:58,067
Then they can bury the
script for this thing.

213
00:06:58,067 --> 00:06:59,733
- [Tom] From the graveyard
of motion pictures,

214
00:06:59,733 --> 00:07:01,467
comes Ring of Terror.

215
00:07:02,567 --> 00:07:03,400
(gentle music)

216
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,867
- [Joel] Funeral group?

217
00:07:04,867 --> 00:07:06,033
- [Crow] Where'd they go?
- [Tom] Funeral guys!

218
00:07:06,033 --> 00:07:06,967
- [Joel] Hey!
- [Tom] Funeral guys!

219
00:07:06,967 --> 00:07:07,933
- [Crow] Where are they hiding?

220
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,433
- [Tom] Where are they?

221
00:07:09,433 --> 00:07:13,800
- [Crow] I told Morris to
bury me in a mausoleum!

222
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,333
- [Joel] Hey!

223
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:17,233
Funeral guys!
- [Tom] Guys?

224
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:19,100
- [Tom] Oh, wait a minute.

225
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:20,167
- [Joel] Hey, guys.

226
00:07:20,167 --> 00:07:21,433
- [Tom] Somebody open that?

227
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:23,100
- [Joel] That thing's
getting really close.

228
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:24,400
- [Crow] Ah, it's
an automatic gate.

229
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,667
It'll open.
- [Tom] Gonna get crushed.

230
00:07:25,667 --> 00:07:26,767
- [Joel] Hey, no,
I don't think so!

231
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:28,033
- [Crow] Yeah!
- [Tom] I'm gonna climb

232
00:07:28,033 --> 00:07:28,967
- [Joel] Hey, hey!
- From over here.

233
00:07:28,967 --> 00:07:29,900
- [Joel] That's not funny!

234
00:07:29,900 --> 00:07:31,233
- [Tom] Hey open that gate!

235
00:07:31,233 --> 00:07:32,033
- [Joel] Hey, do you mind?
(Tom screams)

236
00:07:32,033 --> 00:07:32,833
We're getting too close!

237
00:07:32,833 --> 00:07:33,500
We're gonna crash!

238
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:34,267
Just please, oh!

239
00:07:34,267 --> 00:07:35,433
- [All] Oh!

240
00:07:35,433 --> 00:07:36,300
(robots sigh)

241
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,033
- [Crow] Thank you.

242
00:07:38,033 --> 00:07:40,500
(Joel sighs)

243
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:42,833
- [Joel] Hey, check it out!

244
00:07:42,833 --> 00:07:44,067
Bob Dobson,

245
00:07:44,067 --> 00:07:45,267
from the Church
of the SubGenius!

246
00:07:45,267 --> 00:07:47,833
- [Tom] The Almighty Bob!

247
00:07:47,833 --> 00:07:48,833
- [Joel] Hm.

248
00:07:50,667 --> 00:07:51,933
- [Tom] Hi, I'm the
life of the party.

249
00:07:51,933 --> 00:07:52,733
- [Voiceover] Good
evening, friends.

250
00:07:52,733 --> 00:07:54,233
- [Crow] I'm a lamp!

251
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:56,833
- Let me invite you for a
stroll down Graveyard Lane.

252
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:58,000
- [Joel] Oh, it's Joel Franklin.

253
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,900
- Where beauty and love abide.

254
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:01,800
And in death,

255
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:04,367
we are born to eternal life.

256
00:08:04,367 --> 00:08:05,567
- [Tom] Mr. Magoo!

257
00:08:05,567 --> 00:08:06,500
What happened to you?
(dramatic music)

258
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:08,167
- [Crow] Gloomy Gus!

259
00:08:09,667 --> 00:08:11,167
- [Joel] Ah, life!

260
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,200
(Tom sighs)

261
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:18,367
- All monuments, from the
simplest to the most elaborate,

262
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:22,267
stand erect on the
closed books of the lives

263
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:23,633
of our beloved departed.

264
00:08:23,633 --> 00:08:25,200
- [Joel and Crow] Huh?
- [Tom] What the?

265
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:28,167
And each marker would
hold many stories.

266
00:08:28,167 --> 00:08:31,167
Some filled with happiness.

267
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:32,267
Some

268
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:33,800
filled with sorrow.

269
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,967
- [Joel] Some

270
00:08:34,967 --> 00:08:36,433
filled with a creamy
nougat center!

271
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:39,167
(robots chuckle)

272
00:08:40,367 --> 00:08:42,600
- [Crow] We'll just
wait here, then, huh?

273
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:43,767
Mister?
- [Tom] Uh, hey there?

274
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:44,600
- [Joel] Behind your head?

275
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,733
- [Crow] Hey!

276
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:46,567
- [Tom] Here, yeah.
- [Joel] Hi.

277
00:08:46,567 --> 00:08:48,233
- What would they do

278
00:08:49,433 --> 00:08:51,800
if they had the chance
to relive their lives?

279
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,133
- [Tom] Uh, I'd get out of here.

280
00:08:53,133 --> 00:08:55,267
- [Crow] I'd buy Polaroid.
- [Tom] Yeah.

281
00:08:55,267 --> 00:08:57,333
- What would you do?

282
00:08:57,333 --> 00:08:58,867
- [Tom] Oh, we'd hunt you
down to the ends of the earth,

283
00:08:58,867 --> 00:08:59,700
buddy!

284
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,233
Oh, hi!

285
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,800
- [Joel] Um.
- [Crow] We're over here.

286
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:06,033
(door creaks)

287
00:09:06,033 --> 00:09:06,833
- [Tom] Uh, this way.
- [Joel] Right here.

288
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:07,500
- [Tom] Right down here!

289
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,433
Down here, guy!

290
00:09:08,433 --> 00:09:09,133
Down here!
(Joel mumbles)

291
00:09:09,133 --> 00:09:09,967
- Puma!

292
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,867
- [Tom] What?

293
00:09:11,867 --> 00:09:13,033
- [Joel] Ah, Humor.

294
00:09:13,033 --> 00:09:16,133
You missed that section
on the bookshelf.

295
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,567
Hm?

296
00:09:18,567 --> 00:09:19,700
- [Tom] Uh,

297
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:20,533
we'll just, uh,

298
00:09:20,533 --> 00:09:22,433
stay here, then.

299
00:09:22,433 --> 00:09:23,767
- [Joel] Yoo-ma, hoo-ma?

300
00:09:23,767 --> 00:09:25,300
- [Tom] What's yoo-ma?

301
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,333
Too-ma?

302
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:27,467
Tumor!

303
00:09:27,467 --> 00:09:28,667
He dropped a tumor!
- [Crow] Oh!

304
00:09:28,667 --> 00:09:29,467
He got a tumor
(man calling out)

305
00:09:29,467 --> 00:09:30,267
and he can't find it.

306
00:09:30,267 --> 00:09:31,333
- [Man] Puma!

307
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,467
Hm, I think that's what it's--

308
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:34,400
- [Joel] Let's try the yoo-ma!
- [Man] Puma!

309
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,300
- [Tom] Johnny Yoo-ma. (mumbles)

310
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:36,867
(man mumbles)

311
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:37,867
- [Joel] Ray gun?

312
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:39,167
- [Man] Where are you?

313
00:09:39,167 --> 00:09:41,200
- [Tom] Hm, I don't get it.

314
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:42,300
- [Man] Puma!

315
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:44,000
- [Tom] Oh, yo-yo!

316
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,200
Yo Yo Ma!

317
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,533
It's his favorite cellist!

318
00:09:46,533 --> 00:09:47,667
- [Joel] Ah.
- [Crow] Oh!

319
00:09:47,667 --> 00:09:48,767
- [Crow] In a graveyard?
(dramatic music)

320
00:09:48,767 --> 00:09:49,733
- [Joel] Well--

321
00:09:49,733 --> 00:09:52,400
- [Man] Don't be afraid, Puma!

322
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,600
Don't be afraid!

323
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,467
- [Joel] Ray Hay
Ketchum's buried there.

324
00:09:55,467 --> 00:09:56,400
- [Tom] No.

325
00:09:58,033 --> 00:09:59,767
(ominous music)

326
00:09:59,767 --> 00:10:01,033
- [Man] Puma!

327
00:10:01,033 --> 00:10:03,033
- [Joel] Plot's
around here somewhere.

328
00:10:03,033 --> 00:10:04,167
- [Tom] Huma, I think.

329
00:10:04,167 --> 00:10:05,200
I think, oh--
- [Man] Oh.

330
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,467
- [Man] There you are, Puma!

331
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:07,700
- [Tom] Look!

332
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:08,933
- [Crow] Ah, it's
a little kitty!

333
00:10:08,933 --> 00:10:12,100
- [Man] Nice kitty.
(robot screeches)

334
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:13,833
Yes.
(robot purring)

335
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:15,433
Nice Puma.

336
00:10:15,433 --> 00:10:16,733
- [Crow] Nice kitty.

337
00:10:16,733 --> 00:10:19,733
(robots screech and spit)

338
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:21,733
(all chuckle)

339
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:24,367
- Yes, Puma.
- [Tom] Yes.

340
00:10:24,367 --> 00:10:27,000
Now, let's you and I go
through the storm, huh?

341
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,533
- [Tom] Through the kitchen!

342
00:10:28,533 --> 00:10:30,467
- [Joel] We'll make
a nice burrito!

343
00:10:30,467 --> 00:10:31,833
(cat screeches)

344
00:10:31,833 --> 00:10:33,133
- [Tom] Oh, that's nice.

345
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:35,267
I'm calling Betty White.
- [Man] I'm sorry, Puma.

346
00:10:35,267 --> 00:10:37,033
I didn't mean to step on you!

347
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:39,167
- [Joel] Sure.
- [Tom] Yeah, right!

348
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,733
- [Crow] (screeches)
Run, run this way!

349
00:10:40,733 --> 00:10:41,667
(Tom laughs)

350
00:10:41,667 --> 00:10:43,733
- Puma!
- [Tom] Fuma!

351
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:45,100
Puma!

352
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:46,767
- [Tom] Isn't this a
little redundant, buddy?

353
00:10:46,767 --> 00:10:48,000
- Puma?

354
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
- [Joel] (laughs)
The way he's walking!

355
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,933
(robots chuckle)

356
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:51,033
- [Man] Puma!

357
00:10:51,033 --> 00:10:53,567
- [Crow} (Panting) Think!

358
00:10:53,567 --> 00:10:54,900
Don't tell him where I am!

359
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:55,733
Hide me!

360
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:57,167
- [Man] Don't be afraid!

361
00:10:57,167 --> 00:11:00,067
- [Joel] You're
okay, little fella.

362
00:11:02,033 --> 00:11:03,367
(cat meows)

363
00:11:03,367 --> 00:11:04,200
- [Tom] Caught.

364
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,067
- There, Puma.

365
00:11:06,067 --> 00:11:10,267
Come to (drowned out
by robots screeching)

366
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,700
I didn't mean to step on you!

367
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:15,100
- [Tom] I meant to kill you!

368
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:16,467
(cat meows)

369
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:17,933
- [Tom] Move your head.

370
00:11:17,933 --> 00:11:19,867
- Lewis B. Moffitt.

371
00:11:19,867 --> 00:11:21,133
- [Tom] Sat on a toffit.

372
00:11:21,133 --> 00:11:23,033
- February third, 1933.

373
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,267
November 17, 1955.

374
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,900
- [Tom] If the man
is still alive.

375
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:35,133
- I fear not. (laughs evilly)

376
00:11:35,133 --> 00:11:36,567
- [Tom] I don't think so!

377
00:11:36,567 --> 00:11:39,867
- I remember him.
- [Crow] Mm-hm.

378
00:11:39,867 --> 00:11:41,333
I remember.

379
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:42,167
- [Joel] Yeah?

380
00:11:42,167 --> 00:11:43,567
Tell us about it!

381
00:11:43,567 --> 00:11:44,667
- [Man] Lewis B. Moffitt.
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

382
00:11:44,667 --> 00:11:49,200
(Crow chatters)
(harp strumming)

383
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,433
- [Crow] Hmm.

384
00:11:50,433 --> 00:11:51,133
Buy hand lotion.
(jazzy dance music)

385
00:11:51,133 --> 00:11:52,033
Hm, magazine.

386
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:57,233
- [Tom] Hm, cookie!

387
00:11:57,233 --> 00:12:01,000
- [Joel] Try to get
along with the others!

388
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,867
(Tom's arm rattles)

389
00:12:03,867 --> 00:12:05,533
- Hey, I'm goin'
to the cafeteria!

390
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:07,033
- [Joel] To go get my
forehead lengthened!

391
00:12:07,033 --> 00:12:09,333
- Just waiting for you!
- [Guy] I'm ready!

392
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:10,233
- Come on, dude!

393
00:12:10,233 --> 00:12:11,067
The girls will be there!

394
00:12:11,067 --> 00:12:12,567
- [Tom] Huh?

395
00:12:12,567 --> 00:12:14,500
- [Crow] Geez, Joel, he looks
old to be a college student!

396
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,800
- To the cafeteria!

397
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:16,700
- [Joel] Come on!

398
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:17,800
- Not now.

399
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,267
Maybe later!

400
00:12:19,267 --> 00:12:22,033
- Say, when is your first
lecture in dissection?

401
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:23,367
- It's any day now.

402
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:24,567
- They haven't told us what

403
00:12:24,567 --> 00:12:27,000
everybody's wondering.
(student mumbles)

404
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,800
- Professor Rayburn
is a terrific cut-up!

405
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,667
(gurgles)
(robots laugh)

406
00:12:32,667 --> 00:12:33,500
- [Crow] I love that joke.

407
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,600
- And Gerald McLew?

408
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,900
- Physically, I'm fine.

409
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,133
But technically--

410
00:12:37,133 --> 00:12:38,333
- [Joel] I'm all
messed up inside.

411
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:39,800
- I gotta keep
hitting the books.

412
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,400
- Betty might be
at the cafeteria.

413
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,200
- [Tom] Well, I gotta
keep hitting her, too.

414
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,500
- Ah, go on, let's leave him!

415
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,800
Let's go, fellas!

416
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,400
- [Joel] Yeah, okay, I'm
not into chili peppers,

417
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,233
you know?
- [Tom] Yeah, let's all go.

418
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:49,200
- [Tom] Let's all go.

419
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:49,967
- [Joel] Hate chili peppers.

420
00:12:49,967 --> 00:12:51,200
Love hamburgers.

421
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:51,900
- [Tom] (inhales)
Oh, see, where was I?

422
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:52,633
Oh, yeah.

423
00:12:52,633 --> 00:12:53,900
"See Dick.

424
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,200
"See Dick make a
lateral incision."

425
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:58,667
(upbeat electronic music)

426
00:13:01,367 --> 00:13:03,367
- [Woman] Quite frankly,

427
00:13:03,367 --> 00:13:04,733
I was never so bored
in all my life.

428
00:13:04,733 --> 00:13:05,667
- [Joel] Did you touch it?

429
00:13:05,667 --> 00:13:07,200
- He pulled back on the drive,

430
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,533
and the first thing he did
was turn the car light on.

431
00:13:08,533 --> 00:13:09,367
- On?

432
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,367
(sighs)
- [Joel] That kooks me out!

433
00:13:12,367 --> 00:13:13,600
(robot laughs)

434
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,800
- Then he opened the
glove compartment,

435
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:16,000
took out some papers--

436
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,067
- [Tom] And rolled a big spleef!

437
00:13:17,067 --> 00:13:18,000
- And read me seven chapters

438
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,133
from a book he's writing!

439
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:20,467
- What's the name of the book?

440
00:13:20,467 --> 00:13:21,400
- [Crow] Tropic of Cancer.

441
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,333
- Oh, I remember.

442
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:24,100
He called it the Veet Evolution.

443
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,767
- [Tom] The beef evolution?

444
00:13:25,767 --> 00:13:28,967
- Alice, are you sure there
were no callers for me today?

445
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:30,233
- [Joel] Sorry, Sno-cone.

446
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:31,433
(women mumble)
- [Tom] Who is she Janice Ian?

447
00:13:31,433 --> 00:13:32,400
- [Joel] She looks like a model

448
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:33,833
for Resusci-Annie.

449
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:34,767
- Gee, that's funny.

450
00:13:34,767 --> 00:13:36,100
When Lewis says he'll call,

451
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:37,967
he's always right on the dot.

452
00:13:37,967 --> 00:13:39,367
- [Tom] Yeah, a purple
micro-dot. (chuckles)

453
00:13:39,367 --> 00:13:40,833
- I wonder if anything's wrong.

454
00:13:40,833 --> 00:13:42,067
- Are you kidding?

455
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:43,333
Nothing will ever
happen to that one!

456
00:13:43,333 --> 00:13:44,600
- Why not?

457
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,833
He's just like any
other human being!

458
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:48,900
- [Joel] Well, he's
got a prehensile tail.

459
00:13:48,900 --> 00:13:50,233
- Not from what I hear!

460
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:51,133
- What do you hear, Alice?

461
00:13:51,133 --> 00:13:51,933
- Well,

462
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:56,533
Jerry says he's got
nerves that won't quit.

463
00:13:56,533 --> 00:13:58,967
- My boyfriend Seymour
says he likes him.

464
00:13:58,967 --> 00:13:59,967
- Alice, you were
saying something

465
00:13:59,967 --> 00:14:01,467
I sure wish you'd finish.

466
00:14:01,467 --> 00:14:02,633
- [Tom] It sounds
like it was recorded

467
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,467
in somebody's bathroom,
(women chatter)

468
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,667
doesn't it?

469
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:05,967
- Well, you might not
if you understood.

470
00:14:05,967 --> 00:14:07,167
- Do you understand it?

471
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:09,100
- I think I do!

472
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:10,433
Well, pretty well, anyway.

473
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:11,900
I always get the feeling

474
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:13,733
that there's a fight
going on inside of him.

475
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:14,900
- [Joel] Between
male and female!

476
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,167
- I can't quite sum it to you,

477
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:18,800
but it's like there were
two people inside there,

478
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,033
two separate personalities

479
00:14:20,033 --> 00:14:21,200
trying to gain control.

480
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,333
- [Tom] Glen and Glenda!
(Tom chuckles)

481
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,933
(women mumble)

482
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:27,700
- But I know how I
feel when I'm with him.

483
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:28,933
- Betty, I think you're
in love with him!

484
00:14:28,933 --> 00:14:29,967
- [Crow] I feel
a song coming on!

485
00:14:29,967 --> 00:14:31,600
(Tom sings)

486
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,633
- It could be.

487
00:14:32,633 --> 00:14:35,000
If it weren't for one thing.

488
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,200
- What's that?

489
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,167
- [Joel] I look
like Resusci-Annie.

490
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:38,333
- Nothing seems to shake him!

491
00:14:38,333 --> 00:14:40,267
He's not afraid of anything!

492
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:42,433
It might hurt him someday.

493
00:14:43,833 --> 00:14:44,667
What do you think?

494
00:14:44,667 --> 00:14:46,100
- [All] You're high!

495
00:14:46,100 --> 00:14:48,833
- I'd go crazy trying to
figure the answer to that one!

496
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:50,033
- I'm going to call him!

497
00:14:50,033 --> 00:14:51,400
- [Tom] Oh!

498
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:52,833
Go!

499
00:14:52,833 --> 00:14:55,367
- Well, it's gonna start
getting pretty sticky in here

500
00:14:55,367 --> 00:14:56,300
in a few minutes.
(robots mutter)

501
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:57,867
- [Joel] Let it lay, you guys!

502
00:14:57,867 --> 00:14:59,433
- [Tom] Okay.
(Alice mumbles)

503
00:14:59,433 --> 00:15:01,333
- See you at the cafeteria!

504
00:15:01,333 --> 00:15:02,567
- [Tom] Bye.

505
00:15:02,567 --> 00:15:03,800
- Come on, let's go
to the cafeteria!

506
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,167
- [Joel] Did she say cafeteria?

507
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:06,100
- [Tom] Cafeteria?
- [Crow] Wow!

508
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:09,733
(Joel, Crow and Tom chatter)

509
00:15:11,933 --> 00:15:14,000
(telephone rings)

510
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,300
- [Tom] Uh, could
you get that, son?

511
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,600
Oh, I forget that I
am a college student.

512
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,433
Sorry.

513
00:15:18,433 --> 00:15:19,267
