with his lap?

697
00:21:15,967 --> 00:21:17,733
- [Joel] Hey, music kid?
- [Tom] Use that jaw!

698
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:19,233
- [Joel] Let's go!

699
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:21,067
Play!

700
00:21:21,067 --> 00:21:23,000
(robot slurping)

701
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,967
- [Tom] Boy, I love
these toenail clippings!

702
00:21:24,967 --> 00:21:26,233
- [Crow] Ugh.

703
00:21:26,233 --> 00:21:28,033
- [Joel] Hey, six
inches, everybody!

704
00:21:28,033 --> 00:21:28,867
Come on!

705
00:21:28,867 --> 00:21:30,867
- [Tom] Sorry, split up!

706
00:21:33,467 --> 00:21:35,133
- [Joel] Hi, Grandpa!

707
00:21:35,133 --> 00:21:37,933
- [Crow] Well, here's
your syrup, boys!

708
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:39,433
Chug-a-lug!

709
00:21:39,433 --> 00:21:41,533
What about our pancakes?

710
00:21:41,533 --> 00:21:44,333
- [Tom] Now these
two have a problem.

711
00:21:44,333 --> 00:21:46,800
- Now, which one of the three
sodas did you like the best?

712
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:47,967
- [Crow] Oh, the next one!

713
00:21:47,967 --> 00:21:49,800
- I enjoyed 'em all!
(Tom laughs)

714
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:52,933
I'd like to try a raspberry!

715
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:54,233
- [Joel] Hm!

716
00:21:54,233 --> 00:21:55,433
- You'll have another
one with me? (laughs)

717
00:21:55,433 --> 00:21:57,100
(Crow moans)
(man mumbles)

718
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:57,967
- Well, all right.

719
00:21:57,967 --> 00:21:58,900
Hey, Howard!

720
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:00,133
Give me another one, will ya?

721
00:22:00,133 --> 00:22:01,167
- What is it, Tiny?

722
00:22:01,167 --> 00:22:02,433
- [Tom] Pick me up.

723
00:22:02,433 --> 00:22:03,567
He's trying to hold--
- [Crow] Can I walk?

724
00:22:03,567 --> 00:22:04,100
(robots mumble)
- Make us the raspberry,

725
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:05,400
will ya?

726
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,800
Hey, make it two!

727
00:22:08,367 --> 00:22:10,567
- Two raspberry sodas!

728
00:22:10,567 --> 00:22:12,700
For the last of the
big time spender!

729
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:14,533
(doors clatter)

730
00:22:14,533 --> 00:22:16,467
(flames crackle)
(doors thud)

731
00:22:16,467 --> 00:22:17,300
(engine chugs)

732
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,600
(door slams)

733
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:20,600
(door thuds)

734
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:21,467
(door slams)

735
00:22:21,467 --> 00:22:22,300
(door clatters)

736
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:23,500
- Hey, Cambot,

737
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:24,667
could you run that
music from the movie?

738
00:22:24,667 --> 00:22:25,700
Let's do that thing
we worked out.

739
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:26,900
I got the drawings here.

740
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:27,767
- Okay.

741
00:22:27,767 --> 00:22:28,967
(upbeat music)

742
00:22:28,967 --> 00:22:31,100
Is your college
meeting your needs?

743
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:33,233
Do you find you've plopped
down into the library's

744
00:22:33,233 --> 00:22:36,433
cushy chairs and then
just can't get back up?

745
00:22:36,433 --> 00:22:38,500
- Do you often refer to the
head of the English department

746
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,400
as "Young Man"?

747
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,400
- Do you wish those
frat parties would ditch

748
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,633
