864
00:26:07,433 --> 00:26:08,800
(Lewis chuckles)

865
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:10,333
- I've just had a rendez-vous
with a rattlesnake!

866
00:26:10,333 --> 00:26:12,000
- [Crow] Didja touch it?
- It crawled into the car

867
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:13,367
while we were parked!
(robot grumbles)

868
00:26:13,367 --> 00:26:14,900
But Lewis killed it!

869
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:17,000
- Gee, no wonder she's pale!

870
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,033
- I'd have fainted!

871
00:26:19,033 --> 00:26:20,267
- [Robots] What?

872
00:26:20,267 --> 00:26:22,433
- Lou, I saw Professor
Rayburn on the way down.

873
00:26:22,433 --> 00:26:24,800
He said the coroner might
have a stiff ready for us--

874
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,733
- [Crow] Say, we took
care of that already!

875
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:28,000
- That's great!

876
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:30,000
- Yeah, soon as the City
Coroner confirms it!

877
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,133
He'll let us know
the exact time!

878
00:26:31,133 --> 00:26:32,333
- [Joel] The guy's not dead yet.

879
00:26:32,333 --> 00:26:34,200
He's just really old.
(students mutter)

880
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,667
- [Tom] It's getting better!

881
00:26:35,667 --> 00:26:36,867
- Hey, and maybe it won't
happen tomorrow night.

882
00:26:36,867 --> 00:26:39,233
- [Crow] Let's eat!
- [Joel] Mm-mm!

883
00:26:39,233 --> 00:26:43,300
(students laugh and chatter)

884
00:26:43,300 --> 00:26:44,467
- [Tom] These are baked hams!

885
00:26:44,467 --> 00:26:46,433
And this Karen Fiddly
sent them over!

886
00:26:46,433 --> 00:26:47,267
- Check?

887
00:26:48,633 --> 00:26:50,033
Hey, is this the price,

888
00:26:50,033 --> 00:26:51,700
