all the fleshy tissue--

1259
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:01,967
- [Joel] Around my waist!
(Tom chuckles)

1260
00:38:01,967 --> 00:38:05,167
- This man must have led a
very full and active life.

1261
00:38:05,167 --> 00:38:06,833
- [Crow] 'Cause there's a
squirrel in his stomach!

1262
00:38:06,833 --> 00:38:08,567
(Rayburn mutters)

1263
00:38:08,567 --> 00:38:10,800
- [Rayburn] But his muscle
structure up in his chest--

1264
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:13,600
- [Tom] Oh, cancel that
trip to the White Castle!

1265
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:16,467
- [Joel] Look, I said I'll
never eat Spaghetti-Os!

1266
00:38:16,467 --> 00:38:18,167
- Now, another indication!

1267
00:38:18,167 --> 00:38:20,967
Another indication, gentlemen.

1268
00:38:20,967 --> 00:38:23,233
- [Tom and Joel]
Another indication.

1269
00:38:23,233 --> 00:38:25,467
- [Tom] Another indication.

1270
00:38:26,767 --> 00:38:29,933
- When you look at the--
- [Tom] It's another

1271
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:31,100
- [Tom] indication.
- down here on the right,

1272
00:38:31,100 --> 00:38:32,567
you find, oh, all
kinds of little things.

1273
00:38:32,567 --> 00:38:33,367
- [Crow] Little things like
little cars and trucks,

1274
00:38:33,367 --> 00:38:34,800
little plastic army men.

1275
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:36,000
Lots of fur.
(Rayburn drones)

1276
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:38,900
- [Joel] (grunts) Check please!

1277
00:38:38,900 --> 00:38:40,333
- It's a kind of a dark,

1278
00:38:40,333 --> 00:38:41,333
bloody mass.

1279
00:38:43,300 --> 00:38:46,467
- [Tom] Oh, this
is my stop! (gags)

1280
00:38:46,467 --> 00:38:47,867
- Well, (chuckles) it's not
very pleasant to look at,

1281
00:38:47,867 --> 00:38:49,333
I must admit.

1282
00:38:49,333 --> 00:38:50,700
- [Crow] But with rice
and the correct seasoning,

1283
00:38:50,700 --> 00:38:51,933
you've got a wonderful meal!
(Tom laughs)

1284
00:38:51,933 --> 00:38:55,333
- [Joel] They don't
have nice wrists.

1285
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:58,367
- As we look in the
upper chest cavity--

1286
00:38:58,367 --> 00:39:01,900
- [Tom] Oh, go, please!
(stammers and gags)

1287
00:39:01,900 --> 00:39:02,767
I'm into this.

1288
00:39:02,767 --> 00:39:03,933
It's just the way I am.

1289
00:39:03,933 --> 00:39:07,000
- [Rayburn] The aorta--
- [Crow] The aorta

1290
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:09,167
makes an excellent sock puppet,

1291
00:39:09,167 --> 00:39:10,333
and will, from hereon,

1292
00:39:10,333 --> 00:39:12,367
be represented by the timpani.

1293
00:39:12,367 --> 00:39:15,267
- [Joel] It's 11:00
on the big FM.

1294
00:39:15,267 --> 00:39:16,533
Time for another fade.

1295
00:39:16,533 --> 00:39:18,500
- [Tom] We now find
(Rayburn mumbles)

1296
00:39:18,500 --> 00:39:20,100
Mister Heart.

1297
00:39:20,100 --> 00:39:22,733
It's just a serving
(stutters) suggestion.

1298
00:39:22,733 --> 00:39:25,300
- [Rayburn] Has
rendered posthumously

1299
00:39:25,300 --> 00:39:28,033
a great service to
medical science.

1300
00:39:28,033 --> 00:39:30,033
- [Tom] What a showman,
ladies and gentlemen!

1301
00:39:30,033 --> 00:39:31,533
- [Tom] He gave his all!
- Now he will be transferred

1302
00:39:31,533 --> 00:39:35,267
to the general mausoleum of
the Raven Hills Cemetery.

1303
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:38,100
- [Crow] Where we'll
meet for bars and punch.

1304
00:39:38,100 --> 00:39:39,333
- Where he will be stored

1305
00:39:39,333 --> 00:39:41,033
for about a week

1306
00:39:41,033 --> 00:39:42,900
in the receiving vault.

1307
00:39:42,900 --> 00:39:45,133
- [Tom] These are
the battered faces

1308
00:39:45,133 --> 00:39:46,333
of men in their 40s.

1309
00:39:46,333 --> 00:39:48,033
- [Rayburn] He will
probably be buried there

1310
00:39:48,033 --> 00:39:50,067
in Potter's Field.

1311
00:39:50,067 --> 00:39:51,867
- [Joel] You've been
a wonderful audience!

1312
00:39:51,867 --> 00:39:53,900
Enjoy the buffet!
- [Rayburn] Mister Dumont!

1313
00:39:53,900 --> 00:39:57,467
- You may escort Mister
John Doe to his drawer.

1314
00:39:57,467 --> 00:39:58,667
- [Joel] The junk drawer?

1315
00:39:58,667 --> 00:40:00,700
- [Crow] But first,

1316
00:40:00,700 --> 00:40:02,033
the saw-the-lady-in-half gag!

1317
00:40:02,033 --> 00:40:03,800
(Tom sings)

1318
00:40:03,800 --> 00:40:06,467
(thrilling music)
- [Joel] Oh, no!

1319
00:40:06,467 --> 00:40:08,267
(robots scream)

1320
00:40:08,267 --> 00:40:09,467
- [Crow] It's horrible!
(Tom moans)

1321
00:40:09,467 --> 00:40:10,700
Look at those nails!
(ominous music)

1322
00:40:10,700 --> 00:40:12,467
- [Joel] You were
enjoyed, friend!

1323
00:40:12,467 --> 00:40:14,667
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at
the Amityville House.

1324
00:40:14,667 --> 00:40:19,533
- [Crow] (moans) Not
the clown suit, Dad!

1325
00:40:19,533 --> 00:40:21,100
No!

1326
00:40:21,100 --> 00:40:22,633
I'll take out the trash!
(student mutters)

1327
00:40:22,633 --> 00:40:24,433
Go, Bob, get off of me!

1328
00:40:24,433 --> 00:40:25,667
Oh!

1329
00:40:25,667 --> 00:40:26,500
Oh.

1330
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:30,900
(Tom chortles)

1331
00:40:30,900 --> 00:40:31,733
(Tom growls)

1332
00:40:31,733 --> 00:40:32,567
No.

1333
00:40:32,567 --> 00:40:33,500
Curly.

1334
00:40:33,500 --> 00:40:35,467
- [Joel] Oh, what's this?

1335
00:40:35,467 --> 00:40:38,233
The Psychology of Fear, huh?

1336
00:40:38,233 --> 00:40:39,333
- [Tom] Hm.

1337
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:40,967
(all scream)

1338
00:40:40,967 --> 00:40:44,267
- [Tom] Got me. (sighs)

1339
00:40:47,367 --> 00:40:48,200
Huh.
- [Crow] Hm.

1340
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:49,033
- What is it?

1341
00:40:49,033 --> 00:40:50,267
What's the matter?

1342
00:40:50,267 --> 00:40:51,333
- You were talkin'
in your sleep.

1343
00:40:51,333 --> 00:40:52,167
What's wrong?

1344
00:40:52,167 --> 00:40:53,000
You havin' a nightmare?

1345
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,400
- Oh, (mutters).

1346
00:40:54,400 --> 00:40:56,767
- [Joel] Did I say
anything about a clown suit

1347
00:40:56,767 --> 00:40:57,833
and my uncle?

1348
00:40:59,900 --> 00:41:01,333
- What are you
doin' with my book?

1349
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:03,367
- The Psychology of Fear.

1350
00:41:03,367 --> 00:41:05,367
What are you scared of?

1351
00:41:05,367 --> 00:41:07,267
- [Tom] Give me that!

1352
00:41:07,267 --> 00:41:10,500
And go tell your
mother to come to bed!

1353
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:16,533
- [Crow] Does that
mean I gotta go?

1354
00:41:17,933 --> 00:41:19,000
- [Joel] All right.

1355
00:41:19,000 --> 00:41:20,267
Get in.

1356
00:41:20,267 --> 00:41:21,733
- What's the matter with you?

1357
00:41:21,733 --> 00:41:22,967
- I was just thinking.

1358
00:41:22,967 --> 00:41:24,700
- Do you have to do
it staring at me?

1359
00:41:24,700 --> 00:41:25,967
- [Tom] It helps.

1360
00:41:25,967 --> 00:41:27,000
- You know, every time
you have a nightmare,

1361
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:28,167
you always say the same words.

1362
00:41:28,167 --> 00:41:29,800
"Don't turn off the light."

1363
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:31,133
- What are you doing now?

1364
00:41:31,133 --> 00:41:32,167
Taking notes?

1365
00:41:32,167 --> 00:41:33,700
- What does it mean, anyway?

1366
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,300
- Ask a psychiatrist!

1367
00:41:35,300 --> 00:41:37,300
- Well, don't get touchy!

1368
00:41:37,300 --> 00:41:39,333
- Well, how do
you think it feels

1369
00:41:39,333 --> 00:41:41,033
to wake up and find
some guy staring at you?

1370
00:41:41,033 --> 00:41:42,333
- [Crow] Makes my heart pound.

1371
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:43,867
- I don't mean to
bug you about it.

1372
00:41:43,867 --> 00:41:45,800
- It's the same nightmare
I've been having

1373
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:46,967
ever since I was a kid.

1374
00:41:46,967 --> 00:41:48,233
It's got some meaning, I guess,

1375
00:41:48,233 --> 00:41:49,733
but I don't know what it is.

1376
00:41:49,733 --> 00:41:51,000
- [Joel] I just like it.

1377
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,300
- I may have been around
too many dead bodies.

1378
00:41:52,300 --> 00:41:53,433
Look, if it annoys you,

1379
00:41:53,433 --> 00:41:54,800
I can move to another room.

1380
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:55,833
- Oh, no, I didn't mean that!

1381
00:41:55,833 --> 00:41:57,200
I just, well, you know.

1382
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:58,333
I just wondered.
- [Joel] Yeah.

1383
00:41:58,333 --> 00:41:59,767
- [Tom] He's like totally down.

1384
00:41:59,767 --> 00:42:01,267
- [Tom] Isn't he?
- Don't you get nightmares?

1385
00:42:01,267 --> 00:42:02,600
- After that autopsy, I'll
probably have plenty of 'em.

1386
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:03,633
(robots murmur)

1387
00:42:03,633 --> 00:42:04,600
- Look,

1388
00:42:04,600 --> 00:42:05,833
it's 10 minutes after 4:00.

1389
00:42:05,833 --> 00:42:08,167
- [Tom] And I'm not
even wearing a watch.

1390
00:42:08,167 --> 00:42:09,167
- [Joel] Hm.

1391
00:42:11,967 --> 00:42:13,800
- [Crow] Well, good
night, Sergeant Carter!

1392
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:15,533
- [Joel] Hey, he's turning
the lights off with his mind!

1393
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:16,800
- [Tom] Wow.

1394
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:19,700
(students chatter)
It's the Old School,

1395
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:22,367
where old values are nurtured.

1396
00:42:22,367 --> 00:42:23,633
- [Crow] I don't know about you,

1397
00:42:23,633 --> 00:42:25,167
but that Irene Ryan is fine!
- [Tom] Oo!

1398
00:42:25,167 --> 00:42:27,067
- [Joel] So, we're waitin'
for the CDs to turn over,

1399
00:42:27,067 --> 00:42:28,267
you know?

1400
00:42:28,267 --> 00:42:30,467
Then we're gonna cash 'em.

1401
00:42:32,100 --> 00:42:33,700
- [Tom] Hey, how's the hip, bud?

1402
00:42:33,700 --> 00:42:36,000
You got that cataract
operation comin' up, don't ya?

1403
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:37,167
- [Crow] Yep.

1404
00:42:37,167 --> 00:42:39,233
- [Joel] Hey, speak up.

1405
00:42:39,233 --> 00:42:40,333
Come on.

1406
00:42:40,333 --> 00:42:41,500
That's better.

1407
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:42,767
- Well, not exactly.

1408
00:42:42,767 --> 00:42:43,967
You know, I can't say
I blame them, though.

1409
00:42:43,967 --> 00:42:45,133
We did leave them
stranded at the dance.

1410
00:42:45,133 --> 00:42:46,333
- Alice won't even look at me!

1411
00:42:46,333 --> 00:42:48,067
- [Crow] Can you
blame her, pug boy?

1412
00:42:48,067 --> 00:42:50,400
(Tom sighs)

1413
00:42:52,167 --> 00:42:53,500
- I don't know how
they have the nerve

1414
00:42:53,500 --> 00:42:54,967
to wanna speak to us
even, after last night!

1415
00:42:54,967 --> 00:42:58,967
- I'm tired of playing
second fiddle to a skeleton!

1416
00:43:00,467 --> 00:43:01,900
- Yeah, they'd rather be with
those dead bodies over there

1417
00:43:01,900 --> 00:43:04,033
than with these live
ones right here!

1418
00:43:04,033 --> 00:43:05,267
- [Tom] Tell 'em, Brunhilde!

1419
00:43:05,267 --> 00:43:06,267
- Excuse me.

1420
00:43:08,067 --> 00:43:08,900
- [Joel] (clicks tongue] Uh-oh.

1421
00:43:08,900 --> 00:43:09,833
The monkey boy's coming.

1422
00:43:09,833 --> 00:43:10,667
Excuse me.

1423
00:43:10,667 --> 00:43:12,267
- [Crow] Ditch 'em.

1424
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:16,633
- Betty?

1425
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:18,867
Betty!

1426
00:43:18,867 --> 00:43:19,833
Wait!

1427
00:43:19,833 --> 00:43:20,833
- [Crow] Oh.

1428
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,233
She knows I can't
make those stairs!

1429
00:43:25,233 --> 00:43:26,833
Gotta use the ramp.

1430
00:43:32,033 --> 00:43:33,300
- I was hoping
they'd get over it,

1431
00:43:33,300 --> 00:43:35,167
before we do it again
to them Friday night.

1432
00:43:35,167 --> 00:43:36,433
- That's right!

1433
00:43:36,433 --> 00:43:37,667
The barbecue!

1434
00:43:37,667 --> 00:43:39,133
- [Tom] What, they're
gonna eat the body?

1435
00:43:39,133 --> 00:43:41,333
- When are we gonna get
our initiation assignments?

1436
00:43:41,333 --> 00:43:43,500
- The orders will be handed
to us in sealed envelopes

1437
00:43:43,500 --> 00:43:46,067
at 11:00 PM, after the barbecue.

1438
00:43:46,067 --> 00:43:47,300
- [Joel] Zowie!

1439
00:43:47,300 --> 00:43:48,467
- That oughta be a ball!

1440
00:43:48,467 --> 00:43:49,767
- (scoffs) For whom?

1441
00:43:49,767 --> 00:43:51,267
I hear some pretty
gruesome stories!

1442
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:53,333
- After that autopsy,

1443
00:43:53,333 --> 00:43:54,733
what could be so tough?

1444
00:43:54,733 --> 00:43:56,600
- [Joel] Watching the
fat people eat again?

1445
00:43:56,600 --> 00:43:58,167
- [Crow] Yeah.

1446
00:43:58,167 --> 00:43:59,733
- Hey, you were the only guy
that didn't seem to mind it!

1447
00:43:59,733 --> 00:44:03,433
- Mister Moffit, you may
escort Mister John Doe in.

1448
00:44:03,433 --> 00:44:05,667
Hey, I know what your
initiation assignment should be!

1449
00:44:05,667 --> 00:44:06,833
- Joe.

1450
00:44:06,833 --> 00:44:08,067
- Say it!

1451
00:44:08,067 --> 00:44:09,467
You're thinking
what I'm thinking!

1452
00:44:09,467 --> 00:44:10,300
- [Tom] That makes me psychic!

1453
00:44:10,300 --> 00:44:11,533
- Don't say it!

1454
00:44:11,533 --> 00:44:12,733
We'll suggest it to
the senior committee!

1455
00:44:12,733 --> 00:44:14,000
- Well, I'm game.
- [Joel] Enough said.

1456
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:15,233
- Just so long as I
make the fraternity.

1457
00:44:15,233 --> 00:44:16,533
- [Tom] Yeah.

1458
00:44:16,533 --> 00:44:17,367
Let's go, buddy.

1459
00:44:17,367 --> 00:44:18,700
- [Joel] Yeah, we gotta

1460
00:44:18,700 --> 00:44:19,500
get to class, too.
- [Crow] We're gonna be late.

1461
00:44:19,500 --> 00:44:20,167
- [Student] Let's go!

1462
00:44:20,167 --> 00:44:21,467
See you later!

1463
00:44:21,467 --> 00:44:22,267
(Joel mutters)
- [Tom] Gotta get to class.

1464
00:44:22,267 --> 00:44:23,467
- [Joel] Kill that guy.

1465
00:44:23,467 --> 00:44:25,067
- Boy, if they only knew
what they're in for.

1466
00:44:25,067 --> 00:44:25,900
(senior cackles)

1467
00:44:25,900 --> 00:44:26,733
- Comes the dawn!

1468
00:44:26,733 --> 00:44:27,567
- Brother!

1469
00:44:28,667 --> 00:44:32,167
(upbeat electronic music)

1470
00:44:35,267 --> 00:44:36,867
- All right, gentlemen and miss!

1471
00:44:36,867 --> 00:44:39,233
This is your first exposure

1472
00:44:39,233 --> 00:44:41,633
to the world of robotic
anatomy. (claps)

1473
00:44:41,633 --> 00:44:43,033
Beneath this sheet

1474
00:44:43,033 --> 00:44:45,533
is a one, we will
call Mister Hoover,

1475
00:44:45,533 --> 00:44:47,200
who, through no
fault of his own,

1476
00:44:47,200 --> 00:44:48,433
is dead.
- [Gypsy] Oh.

1477
00:44:48,433 --> 00:44:50,433
He left this world
with one possession,

1478
00:44:50,433 --> 00:44:53,267
an upholstery attachment.
(robots gasping)

1479
00:44:53,267 --> 00:44:54,700
All right, now.

1480
00:44:54,700 --> 00:44:56,600
Keep in mind, this
today's lesson

1481
00:44:56,600 --> 00:44:58,400
will lay the groundwork for your

1482
00:44:58,400 --> 00:45:00,333
future careers in

1483
00:45:00,333 --> 00:45:01,167
medicine,

1484
00:45:02,200 --> 00:45:03,733
or should I say mechanics?

1485
00:45:03,733 --> 00:45:05,767
Some of you will
succeed gloriously,

1486
00:45:05,767 --> 00:45:08,767
while others will
fail miserably.

1487
00:45:08,767 --> 00:45:09,867
Now remember, today's
lesson is in anatomy.

1488
00:45:09,867 --> 00:45:12,600
There will be times when

1489
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,333
you wish to leave the room.

1490
00:45:14,333 --> 00:45:15,733
- [Crow and Tom] Okay, okay.

1491
00:45:15,733 --> 00:45:16,933
- But don't.

1492
00:45:16,933 --> 00:45:18,200
- [Crow] All right.

1493
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:19,467
- All right, now by
examining Mister Hoover,

1494
00:45:19,467 --> 00:45:22,500
we can say he led a very rich

1495
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:24,467
and rewarding existence.

1496
00:45:24,467 --> 00:45:27,733
He inhaled deeply from the
fibers of the carpet of life

1497
00:45:27,733 --> 00:45:31,000
and left the world
a little cleaner.

1498
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:32,667
Now, I carry on a bit,
(abstract pulsing crescendos)

1499
00:45:32,667 --> 00:45:33,967
maybe if you let me go.

1500
00:45:33,967 --> 00:45:35,900
And you can see that...

1501
00:45:39,967 --> 00:45:41,467
It goes like this.

1502
00:45:42,800 --> 00:45:44,067
And it goes like this.

1503
00:45:44,067 --> 00:45:47,067
And leads us up to
(crunches apple).

1504
00:45:47,067 --> 00:45:49,167
The abdominal bag.
(robots gag)

1505
00:45:49,167 --> 00:45:50,633
An incision, okay?

1506
00:45:50,633 --> 00:45:53,900
When you ascend to
