01:07:22,000 --> 01:07:23,767
- [Crow] Oh, really
nice workmanship

2247
01:07:23,767 --> 01:07:26,833
on this gate!
- [Tom] Mm-hm!

2248
01:07:26,833 --> 01:07:28,267
(gate creaks)

2249
01:07:28,267 --> 01:07:29,333
- [Joel] Oh, this
must be a prison.

2250
01:07:29,333 --> 01:07:31,200
Says, "The Come and Bury 'Em."

2251
01:07:31,200 --> 01:07:32,667
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

2252
01:07:32,667 --> 01:07:35,600
- [Crow] Please slip corpses
under the door after 10.

2253
01:07:35,600 --> 01:07:37,900
- [Tom] Kind of a
Louis Sullivan design.

2254
01:07:37,900 --> 01:07:42,633
(haunting organ music)
Hey, listen guys!

2255
01:07:42,633 --> 01:07:44,233
All right!

2256
01:07:44,233 --> 01:07:46,833
It's Procol Harum
doing a sound check!

2257
01:07:46,833 --> 01:07:48,633
- [Joel] Cool.

2258
01:07:48,633 --> 01:07:50,100
- [Tom] Skip the light fandango!

2259
01:07:50,100 --> 01:07:51,833
- [Joel] Hm, they got a
Buddy Squirrel's Nut Shack.

2260
01:07:51,833 --> 01:07:52,667
One potato, two.

2261
01:07:52,667 --> 01:07:53,600
Hot Sam's, Radio Shack?

2262
01:07:53,600 --> 01:07:55,567
This mall's got everything!

2263
01:07:55,567 --> 01:07:59,167
- [Crow] Wow, I wonder what
it costs to heat this barn!

2264
01:07:59,167 --> 01:08:00,933
- [Tom] Verily, I shall sprint

2265
01:08:00,933 --> 01:08:03,900
through the valley of the
shadow of death. (whooshes)

2266
01:08:03,900 --> 01:08:05,700
- [Joel] It actually
says, "You stab 'em,

2267
01:08:05,700 --> 01:08:06,867
"We slab em!"

2268
01:08:06,867 --> 01:08:08,167
That's pretty funny!
(robots laugh)

2269
01:08:08,167 --> 01:08:09,100
At least they got
a sense of humor!

2270
01:08:09,100 --> 01:08:10,900
- [Tom] Yeah.

2271
01:08:10,900 --> 01:08:12,933
- [Crow] Goin' to the chapel.

2272
01:08:12,933 --> 01:08:17,600
Gonna get buried. (chuckles)
- [Tom] Buried.

2273
01:08:17,600 --> 01:08:19,400
- [Tom] (sighs) So
the way I hear it,

2274
01:08:19,400 --> 01:08:20,600
if I smoke one of these things,

2275
01:08:20,600 --> 01:08:22,200
then I'll be able to
join these people, huh?

2276
01:08:22,200 --> 01:08:24,733
- [Joel] Wow, looks
like the EC Escher room!

2277
01:08:24,733 --> 01:08:25,867
- [Tom] MC Escher.

2278
01:08:25,867 --> 01:08:26,700
- [Joel] MC Escher.

2279
01:08:26,700 --> 01:08:27,633
- [Crow] Hey, get me!

2280
01:08:27,633 --> 01:08:29,967
I'm Edward R. Murrow already!

2281
01:08:31,300 --> 01:08:34,033
- [Tom] It's the power station.

2282
01:08:34,033 --> 01:08:35,633
- [Joel] Looks
like a locker room.

2283
01:08:35,633 --> 01:08:37,433
- [Crow] Ah, looks
like HAL's brain.

2284
01:08:37,433 --> 01:08:39,867
- [Joel] Oh, no, I think
it's George Romero's automat.

2285
01:08:39,867 --> 01:08:41,100
- [Tom] Yup, look there.

2286
01:08:41,100 --> 01:08:43,167
There's Hot Hoagie
of the Living Dead.

2287
01:08:43,167 --> 01:08:45,333
- [Joel] Buck and quarter.
(Crow chuckles)

2288
01:08:45,333 --> 01:08:46,433
- [Tom] Cato?

2289
01:08:47,567 --> 01:08:48,633
Where are you, my
little yellow friend?

2290
01:08:48,633 --> 01:08:49,600
Cato?
- [Joel] Cato!

2291
01:08:49,600 --> 01:08:50,433
Cato.

2292
01:08:52,600 --> 01:08:53,667
Oh, good, the kitchen.

2293
01:08:53,667 --> 01:08:54,733
Boy, I'm hungry.

2294
01:08:54,733 --> 01:08:57,333
(robots sniffing)

2295
01:08:57,333 --> 01:08:59,000
- [Joel] Smells like...

2296
01:08:59,000 --> 01:09:01,533
- [Crow] Ah, corpse scat.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2297
01:09:01,533 --> 01:09:04,300
- [Crow] It's around
here somewhere!

2298
01:09:04,300 --> 01:09:06,033
- [Joel] Hm.

2299
01:09:06,033 --> 01:09:07,600
- [Tom] Nice hush puppies.

2300
01:09:07,600 --> 01:09:09,233
- [Joel] Well, Reece's Pieces.

2301
01:09:09,233 --> 01:09:11,467
ET must be on the premises!

2302
01:09:13,867 --> 01:09:15,367
Cato?
- [Tom] Cato?

2303
01:09:16,733 --> 01:09:18,033
- [Crow] Man, this has gotta be

2304
01:09:18,033 --> 01:09:19,767
the biggest place in the world!

2305
01:09:19,767 --> 01:09:20,867
(paper rustles)
- [Tom] Let's see.

2306
01:09:20,867 --> 01:09:21,700
Bread, carrots,

2307
01:09:21,700 --> 01:09:23,000
toilet paper, shaving,

2308
01:09:23,000 --> 01:09:24,600
hey, wait a minute!

2309
01:09:26,733 --> 01:09:27,567
- [Crow] Hm.

2310
01:09:27,567 --> 01:09:29,000
Aisle Three.

2311
01:09:29,000 --> 01:09:33,100
Spices, flour, rice,
corpses, rings of terror.

2312
01:09:33,100 --> 01:09:34,133
(group shouts)

2313
01:09:34,133 --> 01:09:35,500
- [Crow] Merv Griffin!

2314
01:09:35,500 --> 01:09:37,067
What are you doin' here?

2315
01:09:37,067 --> 01:09:38,600
- [Tom] Whoa! (sighs)

2316
01:09:38,600 --> 01:09:39,833
Who died in there?

2317
01:09:39,833 --> 01:09:41,300
- [Joel] Clean up
in Aisle Three!

2318
01:09:41,300 --> 01:09:42,633
- [Tom] (chuckles)
Let me tell ya!

2319
01:09:42,633 --> 01:09:43,767
Let's see, salted.

2320
01:09:43,767 --> 01:09:44,933
Blanched.

2321
01:09:44,933 --> 01:09:47,433
Ah, honey mustard, here we go.

2322
01:09:52,167 --> 01:09:54,367
- [Lewis] A to M.

2323
01:09:54,367 --> 01:09:55,900
Uh.
- [Tom] 18.

2324
01:09:55,900 --> 01:09:59,333
- [Crow] I hate the
Dewey Decimal system!

2325
01:10:00,667 --> 01:10:04,333
- [Tom] Oh, yeah, like
that's a big surprise!

2326
01:10:06,933 --> 01:10:08,333
- [Joel] All right?

2327
01:10:08,333 --> 01:10:09,167
- [Tom] S'okay.

2328
01:10:09,167 --> 01:10:11,700
- [Joel] It's all right.

2329
01:10:11,700 --> 01:10:14,667
- [Tom] Keeps 'em fresh, though.

2330
01:10:14,667 --> 01:10:16,600
- [Joel] Fisher!

2331
01:10:16,600 --> 01:10:18,167
(scary music)

2332
01:10:18,167 --> 01:10:20,567
(robots gagging)

2333
01:10:20,567 --> 01:10:23,100
- [Joel] Oh, God, it reeks!
(Tom gasping)

2334
01:10:23,100 --> 01:10:26,400
- [Crow] Oh, oh, my God, oh, oh!

2335
01:10:26,400 --> 01:10:28,033
Oh, his finger came off!
(Joel and Tom groan)

2336
01:10:28,033 --> 01:10:29,533
Oh, no that's mine!
- [Tom] Gross!

2337
01:10:29,533 --> 01:10:30,900
(cat meows)

2338
01:10:30,900 --> 01:10:33,567
- [Tom] Get that cat outta here!

2339
01:10:34,633 --> 01:10:35,900
(Tom grunts)
- [Joel] What gives?

2340
01:10:35,900 --> 01:10:37,533
- [Crow] Oh.

2341
01:10:37,533 --> 01:10:38,767
- [Joel] What is it, girl?

2342
01:10:38,767 --> 01:10:39,633
Dad?

2343
01:10:39,633 --> 01:10:41,000
He's trapped?

2344
01:10:41,000 --> 01:10:42,233
Down in Dead Rock Canyon?
(door rattles)

2345
01:10:42,233 --> 01:10:44,567
- [Crow] Hey, you
kids, get outta here!

2346
01:10:45,867 --> 01:10:47,867
- [Tom] Let's see,
uh, where was I?

2347
01:10:47,867 --> 01:10:50,733
Oh, yeah, I was about to, uh,

2348
01:10:50,733 --> 01:10:51,567
oh, yeah.

2349
01:10:51,567 --> 01:10:52,933
Oh, oh, God, it's awful!

2350
01:10:52,933 --> 01:10:56,733
Oh, I got my finger! (grunts)

2351
01:10:58,333 --> 01:10:59,633
- [Crow] He's melting!

2352
01:10:59,633 --> 01:11:01,933
- [Joel] Never let
'em see you sweat.

2353
01:11:01,933 --> 01:11:03,000
- [Tom] Nope.

2354
01:11:05,200 --> 01:11:06,633
(cat screeches)

2355
01:11:06,633 --> 01:11:07,467
- [Tom] Whoa!

2356
01:11:07,467 --> 01:11:08,300
- [Crow] Hello Kitty!

2357
01:11:08,300 --> 01:11:09,233
- [Tom and Joel] Oh!

2358
01:11:09,233 --> 01:11:11,300
- [Tom] Oh, remember him?

2359
01:11:12,533 --> 01:11:15,467
(Lewis gasping)
Uh-oh!

2360
01:11:15,467 --> 01:11:16,800
Uh, well,

2361
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:20,000
I guess he won't try that again.

2362
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:20,900
- [Crow] Cat got your tongue?

2363
01:11:20,900 --> 01:11:21,733
- [Joel] I'm Satan.

2364
01:11:21,733 --> 01:11:23,167
I did it and I'm proud!

2365
01:11:23,167 --> 01:11:24,267
(cat meows)
- [Tom] And they said

2366
01:11:24,267 --> 01:11:26,867
those cat guards wouldn't work.

2367
01:11:26,867 --> 01:11:28,033
- [Crow] Please don't haze.

2368
01:11:28,033 --> 01:11:28,867
I'm dead now.

2369
01:11:28,867 --> 01:11:29,700
Don't haze.

2370
01:11:29,700 --> 01:11:30,733
- [Joel] He's 22.

2371
01:11:30,733 --> 01:11:31,900
Yeah, about that.

2372
01:11:31,900 --> 01:11:33,767
- [Tom] Did you
enjoy my little tale?

2373
01:11:33,767 --> 01:11:34,600
Good.

2374
01:11:34,600 --> 01:11:35,767
Kill him!

2375
01:11:35,767 --> 01:11:37,533
- Lewis B. Moffitt.
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

2376
01:11:37,533 --> 01:11:39,433
- I feared not. (chuckles)

2377
01:11:39,433 --> 01:11:40,367
- [Robots] Not!

2378
01:11:40,367 --> 01:11:41,800
- [Tom] (scoffs) That's rich!

2379
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:43,833
- Yet fear dwells
within all of us,

2380
01:11:43,833 --> 01:11:45,667
young and old alike.

2381
01:11:45,667 --> 01:11:47,200
- [Crow] But mostly old.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2382
01:11:47,200 --> 01:11:48,367
- Has terrifying fear

2383
01:11:48,367 --> 01:11:49,233
ever gripped your heart?
- [Joel] That's

2384
01:11:49,233 --> 01:11:50,500
the Kraft tomb.

2385
01:11:50,500 --> 01:11:52,500
That's probably where
Ed Herlihy's buried.

2386
01:11:52,500 --> 01:11:54,000
- [Tom] Uh-oh, geez.

2387
01:11:54,000 --> 01:11:55,200
We've been down this road.
- [Joel] It's that one thing.

2388
01:11:55,200 --> 01:11:56,700
Could somebody please
open the gates?

2389
01:11:56,700 --> 01:11:58,667
- [Crow] Put the brake on.
- [Joel] I'll try to stop 'em!

2390
01:11:58,667 --> 01:12:03,633
(all shouting)
(all murmuring)

2391
01:12:07,633 --> 01:12:09,700
(dramatic orchestral music)
- [Crow] Ninja!

2392
01:12:09,700 --> 01:12:11,900
- [Tom] Well, it looks
like callback time, guys!

2393
01:12:11,900 --> 01:12:12,733
Oh, yeah,

2394
01:12:12,733 --> 01:12:14,733
there he is, Bob Dobson.

2395
01:12:15,967 --> 01:12:18,500
- [Joel] Oh and drive safely!

2396
01:12:18,500 --> 01:12:21,400
Good night!
- [Crow] Sneaky.

2397
01:12:21,400 --> 01:12:22,867
(Crow burbles)

2398
01:12:22,867 --> 01:12:23,800
(robots shriek)

2399
01:12:23,800 --> 01:12:24,733
- [Crow] Let's get outta here!

2400
01:12:24,733 --> 01:12:25,667
It's freaky, man!

2401
01:12:25,667 --> 01:12:28,000
- [Tom] No, it's stupid, man!

2402
01:12:33,433 --> 01:12:36,133
(doors closing)

2403
01:12:42,967 --> 01:12:43,900
- Okay guys.

2404
01:12:43,900 --> 01:12:44,733
It's the end of another movie.

2405
01:12:44,733 --> 01:12:45,567
All you gotta do

2406
01:12:45,567 --> 01:12:46,500
is tell me a good thing

2407
01:12:46,500 --> 01:12:47,967
and get a juicy RAM chip.

2408
01:12:47,967 --> 01:12:49,900
All right?
(Crow sighs)

2409
01:12:49,900 --> 01:12:50,967
- Oh, hold it, Joel!

2410
01:12:50,967 --> 01:12:51,800
This is unfair!

2411
01:12:51,800 --> 01:12:52,633
This film's a dog!

2412
01:12:52,633 --> 01:12:53,500
There isn't an uplifting

2413
01:12:53,500 --> 01:12:54,667
or good thing about it!

2414
01:12:54,667 --> 01:12:55,667
- He' right, Joel.

2415
01:12:55,667 --> 01:12:56,900
Now, for example,

2416
01:12:56,900 --> 01:12:57,733
did you see how
degrading they were

2417
01:12:57,733 --> 01:12:59,000
to overweight people?

2418
01:12:59,000 --> 01:13:00,067
Now it's bad enough they
showed the two fatties

2419
01:13:00,067 --> 01:13:01,633
pounding malts in some desperate

2420
01:13:01,633 --> 01:13:03,800
shark-feeding frenzy,
and eating mountains.

2421
01:13:03,800 --> 01:13:05,733
But then they kept cutting
away to the skinny kids

2422
01:13:05,733 --> 01:13:07,000
laughing as the two tugboats

2423
01:13:07,000 --> 01:13:08,233
tried to tango on
the dance floor!

2424
01:13:08,233 --> 01:13:09,433
RAM chip, please.

2425
01:13:09,433 --> 01:13:10,533
- Yeah, and, uh,
while the other kids

2426
01:13:10,533 --> 01:13:11,500
made out in the bushes,

2427
01:13:11,500 --> 01:13:12,633
our hefty heroes were forced

2428
01:13:12,633 --> 01:13:14,233
to vacuum in a sandwich
with RAM chips.

2429
01:13:14,233 --> 01:13:15,567
And in the very next
scene they showed

2430
01:13:15,567 --> 01:13:16,733
them diving into a wheelbarrow

2431
01:13:16,733 --> 01:13:18,133
full of hot dogs!

2432
01:13:18,133 --> 01:13:19,567
And RAM chips.

2433
01:13:19,567 --> 01:13:20,767
- And it wasn't just
people, either, RAM chip!

2434
01:13:20,767 --> 01:13:22,033
The spooky guy
from the beginning

2435
01:13:22,033 --> 01:13:23,267
purposely stepped on
Puma the cat's tail.

2436
01:13:23,267 --> 01:13:24,100
I'd like my RAM
chip now, please.

2437
01:13:24,100 --> 01:13:25,333
A crispy one.

2438
01:13:25,333 --> 01:13:26,600
- Yeah, and they weren't
using any stunt snake

2439
01:13:26,600 --> 01:13:28,000
when they, guy did the tap dance

2440
01:13:28,000 --> 01:13:28,900
on the rattler's head!

2441
01:13:28,900 --> 01:13:30,100
Uh, RAM chip now?

2442
01:13:30,100 --> 01:13:31,667
- And what about that
car crash victim?

2443
01:13:31,667 --> 01:13:32,500
Onion RAM chip!

2444
01:13:32,500 --> 01:13:33,700
The only two people,

2445
01:13:33,700 --> 01:13:35,300
only two people
show up at his wake.

2446
01:13:35,300 --> 01:13:36,500
And then the only
point of the scene

2447
01:13:36,500 --> 01:13:37,767
was to show how
our hero was really

2448
01:13:37,767 --> 01:13:38,800
a 'fraidy cat, RAM chip now!

2449
01:13:38,800 --> 01:13:40,300
- Yeah!

2450
01:13:40,300 --> 01:13:41,333
So they killed a character
just to advance the plot

2451
01:13:41,333 --> 01:13:42,633
and, oh, geez, Joel.

2452
01:13:42,633 --> 01:13:43,867
What was the deal?

2453
01:13:43,867 --> 01:13:45,100
Are all med students
so mean and frustrated

2454
01:13:45,100 --> 01:13:46,600
'cause they haven't
gotten RAM chips?

2455
01:13:46,600 --> 01:13:47,933
Or just the ones that have
been in school 40 years

2456
01:13:47,933 --> 01:13:49,267
without RAM chips?

2457
01:13:49,267 --> 01:13:50,200
- Well.
- Cherry RAM chips.

2458
01:13:50,200 --> 01:13:51,167
- Listen you have to lighten up

2459
01:13:51,167 --> 01:13:52,500
because, hey, cut it out!

2460
01:13:52,500 --> 01:13:54,733
Because I can think of
an obviously good thing.

2461
01:13:54,733 --> 01:13:56,900
Even though people made
fun of the heavy people,

2462
01:13:56,900 --> 01:13:58,733
they still loved each
other for who they were.

2463
01:13:58,733 --> 01:14:00,100
Now I need something positive

2464
01:14:00,100 --> 01:14:01,367
for you to get a RAM chip.

2465
01:14:01,367 --> 01:14:02,800
- There was tons of
food for them to eat!

2466
01:14:02,800 --> 01:14:04,167
Like chocolate-y RAM chips!

2467
01:14:04,167 --> 01:14:05,900
- Yeah, and this
movie provided work

2468
01:14:05,900 --> 01:14:08,900
for a bunch of senile old
codgers who eat RAM chips!

2469
01:14:08,900 --> 01:14:10,700
- Yeah, none of the
girls had to study late

2470
01:14:10,700 --> 01:14:12,167
or watch dead bodies
getting cut up

2471
01:14:12,167 --> 01:14:13,600
or get a degree,
RAM chip, please.

2472
01:14:13,600 --> 01:14:15,467
- And all the freshmen
were publicly humiliated

2473
01:14:15,467 --> 01:14:16,733
for everyone's enjoyment

2474
01:14:16,733 --> 01:14:18,900
by not getting RAM chips!

2475
01:14:18,900 --> 01:14:20,133
- You're still not giving me

2476
01:14:20,133 --> 01:14:23,300
the positive things I need.
- Oh, hm.

2477
01:14:23,300 --> 01:14:24,533
- Well, at least that guy

2478
01:14:24,533 --> 01:14:26,300
didn't have to
marry Resusci-Annie.

2479
01:14:26,300 --> 01:14:27,933
- Yeah, and thank goodness

2480
01:14:27,933 --> 01:14:29,167
the fat people were so stupid,

2481
01:14:29,167 --> 01:14:30,300
they didn't even
realized they were

2482
01:14:30,300 --> 01:14:31,467
the brunt of everybody's
RAM chip jokes.

2483
01:14:31,467 --> 01:14:32,967
- Yeah.

2484
01:14:32,967 --> 01:14:34,567
Well, it was a good thing
that those mean parents

2485
01:14:34,567 --> 01:14:35,500
locked up our hero

2486
01:14:35,500 --> 01:14:36,433
next to his dead grandad,

2487
01:14:36,433 --> 01:14:38,067
or there wouldn't be a movie,

2488
01:14:38,067 --> 01:14:38,867
or RAM chips.
- That's right.

2489
01:14:38,867 --> 01:14:39,800
- For anyone.

2490
01:14:39,800 --> 01:14:41,000
- Well, listen.
- RAM chips.

2491
01:14:41,000 --> 01:14:42,733
- There's only one
who gets the RAM chip.

2492
01:14:42,733 --> 01:14:44,133
And that's me.
- [Crow] What?

2493
01:14:44,133 --> 01:14:45,267
And I give it to Gypsy.

2494
01:14:45,267 --> 01:14:46,800
(robots shouting)

2495
01:14:46,800 --> 01:14:47,700
There you go, girl.

2496
01:14:47,700 --> 01:14:48,533
All right.

2497
01:14:48,533 --> 01:14:49,733
- Oh, now why, why?

2498
01:14:49,733 --> 01:14:50,933
- Well, because
I'll tell you what.

2499
01:14:50,933 --> 01:14:51,867
The only good thing
about the movie

2500
01:14:51,867 --> 01:14:53,333
was that it was really short!

2501
01:14:53,333 --> 01:14:54,600
- Hey!
- [Crow] Yeah.

2502
01:14:54,600 --> 01:14:55,533
- And we're done for the day!

2503
01:14:55,533 --> 01:14:56,633
- Yeah, we should get a letter.

2504
01:14:56,633 --> 01:14:57,733
(robots cheer)
Get one of those letters

2505
01:14:57,733 --> 01:14:58,933
to read might be--

2506
01:14:58,933 --> 01:14:59,767
- Hold it!

2507
01:14:59,767 --> 01:15:01,233
Don't touch that letter!

2508
01:15:01,233 --> 01:15:02,467
It just so happens

2509
01:15:02,467 --> 01:15:04,933
we've cooked up another
cinematic RAM chip

2510
01:15:04,933 --> 01:15:07,533
for you to digest! (cackles)

2511
01:15:07,533 --> 01:15:08,867
The Phantom Creeps!

2512
01:15:08,867 --> 01:15:09,933
Part Three!

2513
01:15:09,933 --> 01:15:12,300
(all groan)

2514
01:15:13,200 --> 01:15:15,000
- But first, a commercial.

2515
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:17,800
(all wail)

2516
01:15:17,800 --> 01:15:21,300
(upbeat electronic music)

2517
01:15:23,733 --> 01:15:27,833
(dramatic orchestral music)

2518
01:15:27,833 --> 01:15:29,800
- [Joel] Gee, it looks
like an eye chart.

2519
01:15:29,800 --> 01:15:30,633
Doesn't it?

2520
01:15:30,633 --> 01:15:31,867
- [Tom] Yeah.

2521
01:15:31,867 --> 01:15:34,233
I don't think I'm
ready for this.

2522
01:15:36,667 --> 01:15:38,133
Huh.

2523
01:15:38,133 --> 01:15:40,033
- [Crow] Hey, Willis Cooper!

2524
01:15:40,033 --> 01:15:41,767
That's Alice's dad, man!

2525
01:15:41,767 --> 01:15:43,100
- [Tom] No, he was
killed in Vietnam.

2526
01:15:43,100 --> 01:15:44,400
- [Joel] No, he
was Eddie Haskell.

2527
01:15:44,400 --> 01:15:45,400
- [Crow] Oh.

2528
01:15:46,900 --> 01:15:48,367
- [Joel] Hey, what
kind of a Ford

2529
01:15:48,367 --> 01:15:50,033
do you think we'll
have, you guys?

2530
01:15:50,033 --> 01:15:51,467
- [Tom] I think
we'll have a Ford

2531
01:15:51,467 --> 01:15:52,667
- [All] Beebe!

2532
01:15:52,667 --> 01:15:54,167
- [Crow] Ford Beebe!
- [Joel] Beebe!

2533
01:15:54,167 --> 01:15:55,400
(Crow and Tom chant)

2534
01:15:55,400 --> 01:15:56,600
- [Joel] What kind
of Saul do we have?

2535
01:15:56,600 --> 01:16:01,300
- [Tom] Oh, the good
kind of Saul. (chortles)

2536
01:16:02,233 --> 01:16:03,033
- [Crow] To be or not to be!

2537
01:16:03,033 --> 01:16:03,933
Blah, blah, blah!

2538
01:16:03,933 --> 01:16:04,933
That's the question!

2539
01:16:04,933 --> 01:16:06,967
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah!

2540
01:16:06,967 --> 01:16:08,433
- [Joel] Would you get
my agent on the phone?

2541
01:16:08,433 --> 01:16:09,700
I wanna direct!

2542
01:16:11,233 --> 01:16:13,133
- [Tom] And Madonna
has a new look!

2543
01:16:13,133 --> 01:16:14,033
Come on, Vogue.

2544
01:16:14,033 --> 01:16:15,000
There's nothing to it!

2545
01:16:15,000 --> 01:16:15,933
Strike a pose!

2546
01:16:15,933 --> 01:16:17,000
- [Joel] Steven, did you think

2547
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:18,567
Grandpa seemed funny this trip?

2548
01:16:18,567 --> 01:16:19,400
- [Crow] Punch it, Hale.

2549
01:16:19,400 --> 01:16:21,300
I wanna die with you!

2550
01:16:21,300 --> 01:16:23,400
- [Tom] Dumpy and frumpy!

2551
01:16:24,767 --> 01:16:27,133
(chuckles) A good one!

2552
01:16:27,133 --> 01:16:28,067
- [Joel] And, of course,

2553
01:16:28,067 --> 01:16:29,567
the boys in the back room.

2554
01:16:29,567 --> 01:16:32,367
- [Crow] Vandegrift Generator!
(Tom mumbles)

2555
01:16:32,367 --> 01:16:33,300
- [Joel] Dora Clementine!

2556
01:16:33,300 --> 01:16:34,567
- [Crow] Hugh Chet Huntley!

2557
01:16:34,567 --> 01:16:36,033
- [Tom] Anthony
Averill Harriman.

2558
01:16:36,033 --> 01:16:36,967
- [Joel] Frank Mayo Brothers.

2559
01:16:36,967 --> 01:16:37,700
- [Crow] James Gnarly Farley.

2560
01:16:37,700 --> 01:16:38,533
- [Tom] Rosebud.

2561
01:16:38,533 --> 01:16:39,933
Rosebud, rosebud.

2562
01:16:41,800 --> 01:16:43,133
- [Joel] Trying to
keep the credits down!

2563
01:16:43,133 --> 01:16:44,800
- [Crow] Well,
foreword is forwarned.

2564
01:16:44,800 --> 01:16:46,300
Doctor Zorka, not a real doctor,

2565
01:16:46,300 --> 01:16:48,000
but believed to be dead,

2566
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:50,167
attempts to prevent
the authorities

2567
01:16:50,167 --> 01:16:51,167
from discovering

2568
01:16:51,167 --> 01:16:52,600
his scientific secrets,

2569
01:16:52,600 --> 01:16:53,833
the Helsinki formula,

2570
01:16:53,833 --> 01:16:56,067
by using a device which
makes him invisible,

2571
01:16:56,067 --> 01:16:59,333
a contract to appear on the
Comedy Channel. (laughs)

2572
01:16:59,333 --> 01:17:03,067
I guess I'm outta here.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2573
01:17:03,067 --> 01:17:04,867
- [Joel] Now, Doctor Mallory

2574
01:17:04,867 --> 01:17:07,433
will be represented by the oboe.

2575
01:17:07,433 --> 01:17:09,300
And when you hear
the scary oboe sound,

2576
01:17:09,300 --> 01:17:12,500
stomp your feet and go, "Boo!"

2577
01:17:12,500 --> 01:17:14,700
(Tom moans)

2578
01:17:14,700 --> 01:17:16,500
- [Tom] Nancy's sister, Jean,

2579
01:17:16,500 --> 01:17:18,333
will look around.

2580
01:17:18,333 --> 01:17:20,100
- [Joel] Hey, what's this?

2581
01:17:20,100 --> 01:17:21,333
- [Crow] Get that
frog outta here!

2582
01:17:21,333 --> 01:17:22,300
- [Joel] Hey!

2583
01:17:22,300 --> 01:17:23,600
Huh, somebody left a mint.

2584
01:17:23,600 --> 01:17:26,167
- [Tom] A welcome to
the Embassy sweet.

2585
01:17:26,167 --> 01:17:28,033
- [Joel] Heh, let's see.

2586
01:17:28,033 --> 01:17:30,333
- [Tom] Take that.

2587
01:17:30,333 --> 01:17:32,033
(Tom mutters)

2588
01:17:32,033 --> 01:17:34,333
- [Crow] Checkin'
the bush, boss!

2589
01:17:34,333 --> 01:17:35,500
- [Joel] A coin.

2590
01:17:35,500 --> 01:17:36,633
A car.

2591
01:17:36,633 --> 01:17:38,900
- [Crow] Joyride time!
- [Tom] Yeah!

2592
01:17:38,900 --> 01:17:40,833
(robots hoot and sing)

2593
01:17:40,833 --> 01:17:43,267
- [Crow] Eat my dust!

2594
01:17:43,267 --> 01:17:45,833
- [Joel] Hey, it looks
like an ear of corn!

2595
01:17:45,833 --> 01:17:48,900
(robots grunt)

2596
01:17:48,900 --> 01:17:49,967
Why, I think I heard

2597
01:17:49,967 --> 01:17:51,833
a floating ear of corn!

2598
01:17:51,833 --> 01:17:52,967
(stick thuds)
- [Tom] Oof.

2599
01:17:52,967 --> 01:17:53,900
- [Joel] Yup.

2600
01:17:53,900 --> 01:17:54,767
- [Tom] Ooh, that had to hurt.

2601
01:17:54,767 --> 01:17:55,967
Yeah, you know.

2602
01:17:55,967 --> 01:17:57,433
They're always
repeating these things

2603
01:17:57,433 --> 01:17:58,767
on America's Funniest
Home Videos, aren't they?

2604
01:17:58,767 --> 01:18:00,433
- [Crow] Yeah.
- [Joel] Well.

2605
01:18:00,433 --> 01:18:01,267
(truck rumbles)
- [Robots] Goodbye!

2606
01:18:01,267 --> 01:18:02,167
- [Tom ] So long!

2607
01:18:02,167 --> 01:18:03,433
Feeder-zane!

2608
01:18:03,433 --> 01:18:04,367
Don't forget to write!
- [Joel] Don't forget

2609
01:18:04,367 --> 01:18:05,033
to throw the kitchen sinks!

2610
01:18:05,033 --> 01:18:05,833
- [Tom] Bye!

2611
01:18:05,833 --> 01:18:07,033
See you next fall!

2612
01:18:07,033 --> 01:18:07,700
- [Crow] Does that
mean the date's over?

2613
01:18:07,700 --> 01:18:08,933
(Tom chuckles)

2614
01:18:08,933 --> 01:18:09,867
- [Tom] Well, that
must be the part

2615
01:18:09,867 --> 01:18:10,667
they didn't show us there.

2616
01:18:10,667 --> 01:18:11,333
(explosion blasts)

2617
01:18:11,333 --> 01:18:12,133
- [All] Oh!

2618
01:18:12,133 --> 01:18:14,100
- [Tom] Nice tag!

2619
01:18:14,100 --> 01:18:15,933
- [Joel] I'm gonna
try that, too!

2620
01:18:15,933 --> 01:18:17,267
I'm going to join him

2621
01:18:17,267 --> 01:18:18,500
in death!
- [Crow] Okay.

2622
01:18:18,500 --> 01:18:19,533
- [Crow] You just
go really fast and--

2623
01:18:19,533 --> 01:18:21,167
- [Tom] Go for it!
Oh!

2624
01:18:21,167 --> 01:18:23,133
Oh, yeah, he's okay.

2625
01:18:23,133 --> 01:18:25,800
- [Joel] Always clownin' around.

2626
01:18:26,700 --> 01:18:27,533
- [Tom] Come on.

2627
01:18:27,533 --> 01:18:28,700
Get in, dummy!

2628
01:18:29,700 --> 01:18:32,267
(sighs) I'm sorry, Mom.

2629
01:18:32,267 --> 01:18:34,600
I'll take out the
garbage next week!

2630
01:18:34,600 --> 01:18:35,833
I'm sorry!
(frogs croak)

2631
01:18:35,833 --> 01:18:37,167
- There's something
over in those bushes!

2632
01:18:37,167 --> 01:18:38,533
- [Tom] It's a frog.

2633
01:18:38,533 --> 01:18:40,233
- [Man] Keep down.
- [Joel] Invisible frog.

2634
01:18:40,233 --> 01:18:41,600
- Did you see the
driver of that car?

2635
01:18:41,600 --> 01:18:42,433
(gunshot blasts)

2636
01:18:42,433 --> 01:18:43,300
- [Tom] Oh, good, Bob.

2637
01:18:43,300 --> 01:18:44,133
You killed a Sequoia.

2638
01:18:44,133 --> 01:18:45,367
- Whatever it is.

2639
01:18:45,367 --> 01:18:47,300
- [Joel] I bet he
misses you, too!

2640
01:18:47,300 --> 01:18:49,533
- Let's get to your car!

2641
01:18:49,533 --> 01:18:52,300
- [Tom] Yeah, it's
better than mine.

2642
01:18:52,300 --> 01:18:54,267
- That's one, shoot it!

2643
01:18:54,267 --> 01:18:55,567
- [Tom] The itsy bitsy, whoa?

2644
01:18:55,567 --> 01:18:56,800
- Shoes don't lie.

2645
01:18:56,800 --> 01:18:57,733
That's one of Zorka's
mechanical devices!

2646
01:18:57,733 --> 01:18:58,567
- [Joel] Say!

2647
01:18:58,567 --> 01:19:00,333
- But it's poisonous!

2648
01:19:00,333 --> 01:19:01,433
- What are you going to do?

2649
01:19:01,433 --> 01:19:02,633
- Try and catch it

2650
01:19:02,633 --> 01:19:04,633
to take it to
Mallory for analysis.

2651
01:19:04,633 --> 01:19:05,867
(explosion blasts)

2652
01:19:05,867 --> 01:19:07,633
- [Crow] Oh, he used
a smoking jacket!

2653
01:19:07,633 --> 01:19:09,433
- It's not like our hard-boiled
chief for a girl to faint!

2654
01:19:09,433 --> 01:19:12,133
- I'm not a girl.
- [Joel] No I'm soft-boiled.

2655
01:19:12,133 --> 01:19:14,433
- [Crow] She's poached.

2656
01:19:14,433 --> 01:19:17,100
- [Joel] I thought I'd
never get out of this field.

2657
01:19:17,100 --> 01:19:18,700
'Scuse me!

2658
01:19:18,700 --> 01:19:19,533
(whistling)

2659
01:19:19,533 --> 01:19:20,400
That's Uncle Joe.

2660
01:19:20,400 --> 01:19:23,133
He's moving kinda slow.

2661
01:19:23,133 --> 01:19:25,800
- [Tom] He has stylee-tick-thus!

2662
01:19:27,300 --> 01:19:29,867
(Joel singing)

2663
01:19:31,033 --> 01:19:32,400
(engine revving)

2664
01:19:32,400 --> 01:19:33,600
- [Crow] Please!

2665
01:19:33,600 --> 01:19:35,933
At least let me
get the tie rod in!

2666
01:19:35,933 --> 01:19:38,367
- [Tom] Next week, I go
to the ladies' locker room

2667
01:19:38,367 --> 01:19:39,367
at the YWCA!

2668
01:19:40,967 --> 01:19:43,467
- [Joel] They say I make a
better door than a window!

2669
01:19:43,467 --> 01:19:44,633
(Tom laughs)

2670
01:19:44,633 --> 01:19:45,433
Now I kill something
for no reason.

2671
01:19:45,433 --> 01:19:46,367
- Don't worry, I will.

2672
01:19:46,367 --> 01:19:47,033
I have a hunch one of those

2673
01:19:47,033 --> 01:19:48,300
got to Jim Daly.

2674
01:19:48,300 --> 01:19:49,133
- [Tom] Oh, that's why
he's doing show tunes

2675
01:19:49,133 --> 01:19:50,100
all the time.

2676
01:19:50,100 --> 01:19:51,600
- It's gone!

2677
01:19:51,600 --> 01:19:53,000
- [Crow] Make sure you get
a dry cleaning receipt!

2678
01:19:53,000 --> 01:19:54,533
- Where'd it go?

2679
01:19:54,533 --> 01:19:55,800
- I don't know.

2680
01:19:55,800 --> 01:19:58,067
I wish I knew
where it came from.

2681
01:19:58,067 --> 01:20:00,700
- [Tom] You folks know?

2682
01:20:00,700 --> 01:20:02,200
- That may be Mallory now!

2683
01:20:02,200 --> 01:20:04,200
- [Joel] No, it's
the copper top.

2684
01:20:04,200 --> 01:20:05,700
(Tom sings)
- It is Mallory!

2685
01:20:05,700 --> 01:20:06,933
Two of my men!

2686
01:20:06,933 --> 01:20:08,067
- [Crow] Two of my
good strong men!

2687
01:20:08,067 --> 01:20:09,533
- [Tom] Yes!

2688
01:20:09,533 --> 01:20:10,800
- You all right, Bob?

2689
01:20:10,800 --> 01:20:12,500
- [Tom] Yeah, but
my coat's wrecked.

2690
01:20:12,500 --> 01:20:13,900
- They arrived just in time!

2691
01:20:13,900 --> 01:20:16,033
Parker, check that
car for ownership.

2692
01:20:16,033 --> 01:20:17,233
If there's enough left of it.

2693
01:20:17,233 --> 01:20:18,533
- [Joel] Yeah, it's registered

2694
01:20:18,533 --> 01:20:19,767
under the name Beelzebub.

2695
01:20:19,767 --> 01:20:20,933
- Miss Drew would
like to go, too.

2696
01:20:20,933 --> 01:20:22,367
She'll take you back in her car,

2697
01:20:22,367 --> 01:20:23,200
won't you?

2698
01:20:23,200 --> 01:20:24,733
- But!

2699
01:20:24,733 --> 01:20:25,967
- A lot of this case has
to be kept off the record.

2700
01:20:25,967 --> 01:20:26,900
- [Crow] Yeah, but
it'll fit on the CD

2701
01:20:26,900 --> 01:20:28,133
on the extra bonus track.

2702
01:20:28,133 --> 01:20:29,067
- It's like we've left
something behind us,

2703
01:20:29,067 --> 01:20:30,600
even worse than dynamite!

2704
01:20:30,600 --> 01:20:31,800
- [Joel] This film?

2705
01:20:31,800 --> 01:20:32,967
- Someone evidently
got hold of it.

2706
01:20:32,967 --> 01:20:34,133
The wrong kind of
publicity will hurt him.

2707
01:20:34,133 --> 01:20:35,367
- All right.

2708
01:20:35,367 --> 01:20:36,200
I'll be careful what
I phone the paper.

2709
01:20:36,200 --> 01:20:37,133
- That's swell.

2710
01:20:37,133 --> 01:20:38,400
I knew I could count on you.

2711
01:20:38,400 --> 01:20:39,400
Check with me and
Mallory tomorrow.

2712
01:20:39,400 --> 01:20:40,633
- [Jean] Thanks, I will.

2713
01:20:40,633 --> 01:20:42,167
- What's the matter
with your coat?

2714
01:20:42,167 --> 01:20:43,433
- One of the Doctor's
mechanical spiders

2715
01:20:43,433 --> 01:20:44,400
disappeared under it.

2716
01:20:44,400 --> 01:20:45,367
I don't dare put it on.

2717
01:20:45,367 --> 01:20:46,467
- Why, how'd it get out here?

2718
01:20:46,467 --> 01:20:47,967
- I wish you'd tell me.

2719
01:20:47,967 --> 01:20:49,733
I chased that car from Zorka
and the driver got away.

2720
01:20:49,733 --> 01:20:51,067
- [Crow] Try not
to talk so fast!

2721
01:20:51,067 --> 01:20:52,033
- I'll look around for him--

2722
01:20:52,033 --> 01:20:52,867
- [Tom] A bunch of auctioneers.

2723
01:20:52,867 --> 01:20:54,133
- No, it's too late.

2724
01:20:54,133 --> 01:20:55,100
He's probably miles
away from here by now.

2725
01:20:55,100 --> 01:20:56,367
Let's get back to Zorka's!

2726
01:20:56,367 --> 01:20:57,567
- There's an extra
mac in the car here!

2727
01:20:57,567 --> 01:20:59,367
- [Joel] Oh, great,
I'm famished!

2728
01:20:59,367 --> 01:21:01,367
- [Tom] Hey, hey, where'd
you learn how to drive?

2729
01:21:01,367 --> 01:21:03,500
Those shocks are terrible!

2730
01:21:05,100 --> 01:21:06,333
- It's Monk!

2731
01:21:06,333 --> 01:21:08,767
- [Joel] One of
the jazz murders!

2732
01:21:08,767 --> 01:21:09,767
- This is a break!

2733
01:21:09,767 --> 01:21:10,967
The chief wants him!

2734
01:21:10,967 --> 01:21:13,567
Let's see if we
can bring him, too.

2735
01:21:17,967 --> 01:21:19,100
Listen, Monk,

2736
01:21:19,100 --> 01:21:20,667
with Zorka dead,
you're in a tough spot!

2737
01:21:20,667 --> 01:21:21,667
Now why don't you
join up with our crowd

2738
01:21:21,667 --> 01:21:22,800
and tell us what's become

2739
01:21:22,800 --> 01:21:24,067
of Zorka's farmhouse!
(Tom mutters)

2740
01:21:24,067 --> 01:21:25,733
- What makes you think I
know anything about it?

2741
01:21:25,733 --> 01:21:27,133
- [Tom] Well, I oughta pop you!

2742
01:21:27,133 --> 01:21:28,667
- [Joel] How would you
like a knuckle sandwich,

2743
01:21:28,667 --> 01:21:30,200
Mister Frank Mayo?
(men mumble)

2744
01:21:30,200 --> 01:21:31,367
- [Bob] Quit stalling!

2745
01:21:31,367 --> 01:21:33,600
You know what we're
talking about!

2746
01:21:33,600 --> 01:21:36,100
- I can't even guess!
(Tom chuckles)

2747
01:21:36,100 --> 01:21:37,333
- All right.

2748
01:21:37,333 --> 01:21:38,767
We'll take him along
and work him over.

2749
01:21:38,767 --> 01:21:40,000
- [Joel] Great!

2750
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:41,933
I've been wanting
to drop some pounds!

2751
01:21:41,933 --> 01:21:42,867
- [Tom] Oh!

2752
01:21:42,867 --> 01:21:44,200
Liston is down, Liston is down!

2753
01:21:44,200 --> 01:21:48,000
Cassius Clay is the
new world champion!

2754
01:21:48,000 --> 01:21:48,967
- Get in the car quick!

2755
01:21:48,967 --> 01:21:51,200
Come on, you guys!

2756
01:21:51,200 --> 01:21:52,600
- [Crow] Ghost
car to the rescue!

2757
01:21:52,600 --> 01:21:53,833
- [Tom] Yay!

2758
01:21:53,833 --> 01:21:55,267
- [Crow] Oh, look,
no jackrabbit starts!

2759
01:21:55,267 --> 01:21:57,033
Oh! (grunts)

2760
01:21:57,033 --> 01:21:58,000
- [Tom] Right.

2761
01:21:58,000 --> 01:21:58,967
Drive along this river junction!

2762
01:21:58,967 --> 01:22:00,233
Take a left at the cyclorama!

2763
01:22:00,233 --> 01:22:01,200
- They've taken their
prisoner with them!

2764
01:22:01,200 --> 01:22:02,500
- Where do you suppose they are?

2765
01:22:02,500 --> 01:22:03,733
- Well, we're gonna find out!

2766
01:22:03,733 --> 01:22:06,167
- [Crow] That's
not what I asked!

2767
01:22:08,100 --> 01:22:08,933
Whoa!

2768
01:22:10,567 --> 01:22:12,233
♪ The Getaway Chase Game ♪

2769
01:22:12,233 --> 01:22:13,733
♪ Getaway ♪

2770
01:22:13,733 --> 01:22:14,667
- [Crow] Gotta
getaway, gotta getaway!

2771
01:22:14,667 --> 01:22:15,600
- [Tom] We don't know who it is.

2772
01:22:15,600 --> 01:22:16,400
Let's just shoot all the tires

2773
01:22:16,400 --> 01:22:17,967
and let God sort it out.

2774
01:22:17,967 --> 01:22:20,700
- [Joel] Let God patch it.

2775
01:22:20,700 --> 01:22:21,667
- [Crow] What!

2776
01:22:21,667 --> 01:22:22,600
Oh, guy!

2777
01:22:22,600 --> 01:22:23,467
You gotta know how to ease down!

2778
01:22:23,467 --> 01:22:24,300
This is a big car!

2779
01:22:24,300 --> 01:22:25,533
Come on!

2780
01:22:25,533 --> 01:22:26,800
- [Joel] I woulda
put on my belt,

2781
01:22:26,800 --> 01:22:30,200
but they hadn't been
invented yet, boss!

2782
01:22:30,200 --> 01:22:32,867
- [Tom] Ghost car to the rescue.

2783
01:22:34,333 --> 01:22:35,567
Oh, let's have a picnic!

2784
01:22:35,567 --> 01:22:36,400
Come on!

2785
01:22:37,667 --> 01:22:38,667
Ooh!

2786
01:22:38,667 --> 01:22:39,900
Come here, you!

2787
01:22:39,900 --> 01:22:41,000
I love you, you're
mine! (giggles)

2788
01:22:41,000 --> 01:22:41,833
Quit tickling.
- [Joel] Hey!

2789
01:22:41,833 --> 01:22:43,267
Cut it out! (giggles)

2790
01:22:43,267 --> 01:22:44,533
- [Crow] Yeah, eat
it, boy, eat it!

2791
01:22:44,533 --> 01:22:45,900
Die, boy, die!

2792
01:22:45,900 --> 01:22:47,867
Eat it, swallow it!
- [Joel] No don't drool on me!

2793
01:22:47,867 --> 01:22:49,033
- [Tom] He's gonna snag on ya.

2794
01:22:49,033 --> 01:22:50,267
He's gonna snag on you!

2795
01:22:50,267 --> 01:22:53,200
(muffled shouting)

2796
01:22:55,433 --> 01:22:57,033
- Now, who are ya?

2797
01:22:57,033 --> 01:22:59,100
What were you doing
at Zorka's house?

2798
01:22:59,100 --> 01:23:00,233
Come on, talk up!

2799
01:23:00,233 --> 01:23:01,333
- Well, I--
- [Joel] I, uh, uh...

2800
01:23:01,333 --> 01:23:02,300
(gunshot blasts)

2801
01:23:02,300 --> 01:23:03,833
- [Tom] Oh!

2802
01:23:03,833 --> 01:23:04,833
I guess they didn't want
him to spill the beans, huh?

2803
01:23:04,833 --> 01:23:06,433
- [Joel] He's always stunned.

2804
01:23:06,433 --> 01:23:08,000
- [Crow] Joel, how come
they kill all these people,

2805
01:23:08,000 --> 01:23:08,933
but the credits don't
get any shorter?

2806
01:23:08,933 --> 01:23:10,433
(gunshots blasting)

2807
01:23:10,433 --> 01:23:12,133
- [Tom] Have you noticed all
these guys look the same?

2808
01:23:12,133 --> 01:23:14,067
How do they know who
they're shooting at?

2809
01:23:14,067 --> 01:23:15,300
- [Crow] Okay, you
proved your point.

2810
01:23:15,300 --> 01:23:16,967
- [Tom] Yup.

2811
01:23:16,967 --> 01:23:19,067
- Shall I go get 'em?

2812
01:23:19,067 --> 01:23:20,800
- No, it's too late.

2813
01:23:20,800 --> 01:23:22,167
We got one of 'em anyway.

2814
01:23:22,167 --> 01:23:23,333
You've been very good!

2815
01:23:23,333 --> 01:23:25,500
- [Joel] No, he's our guy.

2816
01:23:28,000 --> 01:23:30,467
- They fixed this
one so he won't talk.

2817
01:23:30,467 --> 01:23:32,100
- Sure is good shootin'
for this kinda light.

2818
01:23:32,100 --> 01:23:35,600
- [Tom] Yeah, I
gotta admire him.

2819
01:23:35,600 --> 01:23:36,833
- Are you men all right?

2820
01:23:36,833 --> 01:23:38,067
- Sure thing!

2821
01:23:38,067 --> 01:23:39,267
- [Joel] We got him!

2822
01:23:39,267 --> 01:23:40,200
- We're trying to print
some measurements--

2823
01:23:40,200 --> 01:23:41,467
- [Crow] It's kinda light.

2824
01:23:41,467 --> 01:23:42,600
- [Joel] I'd like
to shake his hand!

2825
01:23:42,600 --> 01:23:43,267
- I'll get the equipment
out of the car.

2826
01:23:43,267 --> 01:23:44,533
- [Tom] Yeah.

2827
01:23:44,533 --> 01:23:45,200
- We gotta find out
all about this gang.

2828
01:23:45,200 --> 01:23:46,400
Who they are

2829
01:23:46,400 --> 01:23:47,900
and what they're doing
in this business.

2830
01:23:47,900 --> 01:23:49,433
- [Tom] Why do they shoot
each other all the time?

2831
01:23:49,433 --> 01:23:50,367
- Those men are who Zorka
is selling his formula to.

2832
01:23:50,367 --> 01:23:52,533
- That's what I'm afraid of.

2833
01:23:53,567 --> 01:23:54,833
- [Joel] That guy's right!

2834
01:23:54,833 --> 01:23:57,933
He really does have
a flat butt, boss!

2835
01:24:01,933 --> 01:24:03,800
- [Tom] Hm, nice watch.

2836
01:24:06,600 --> 01:24:08,267
- So, you were
going to sell me out

2837
01:24:08,267 --> 01:24:10,167
to (mumbles), were you?

2838
01:24:10,167 --> 01:24:11,000
- [Tom] No, boss!

2839
01:24:11,000 --> 01:24:12,267
I love you, I swear!

2840
01:24:12,267 --> 01:24:13,533
Oh, you're kidding!

2841
01:24:13,533 --> 01:24:14,833
That's a...
(Monk mutters)

2842
01:24:14,833 --> 01:24:16,033
- Of course.

2843
01:24:16,033 --> 01:24:18,500
You wouldn't dare to betray me.

2844
01:24:18,500 --> 01:24:20,467
The police still want you, Monk!

2845
01:24:20,467 --> 01:24:21,767
They don't want me!

2846
01:24:21,767 --> 01:24:22,633
- [Joel] Mong?

2847
01:24:22,633 --> 01:24:24,633
- They think I'm dead!

2848
01:24:24,633 --> 01:24:25,733
- [Joel] You are.

2849
01:24:25,733 --> 01:24:27,400
- Now the government and the spy

2850
01:24:27,400 --> 01:24:29,700
are both determined
to steal my secret!

2851
01:24:29,700 --> 01:24:32,633
It is necessary to
share a very vital

2852
01:24:32,633 --> 01:24:34,167
secret knowledge with you!

2853
01:24:34,167 --> 01:24:35,667
- [Crow] I like to
wear the mittens!

2854
01:24:35,667 --> 01:24:38,133
- The hiding place of the
source of all my power.

2855
01:24:38,133 --> 01:24:39,067
- [Monk] The source!

2856
01:24:39,067 --> 01:24:39,800
- [Tom] Cool, let me at it!

2857
01:24:39,800 --> 01:24:41,133
- [Crow] Wow.

2858
01:24:41,133 --> 01:24:42,433
Hey, is that where you make

2859
01:24:42,433 --> 01:24:43,933
those great baked beans?

2860
01:24:43,933 --> 01:24:48,133
- [Tom] Whistleberries you
must never taste! (chuckles)

2861
01:24:48,133 --> 01:24:50,533
Uh, boss, I'm fine, really.

2862
01:24:50,533 --> 01:24:52,500
Uh, I checked myself
at home in the shower.

2863
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:55,733
You don't have to,
uh, oh. (sighs)

2864
01:24:55,733 --> 01:24:56,767
- [Crow] That was close.

2865
01:24:56,767 --> 01:24:57,867
- [Tom] Yeah.

2866
01:24:59,133 --> 01:25:00,867
It's called the Rubics cube!

2867
01:25:00,867 --> 01:25:01,967
Don't screw it up!

2868
01:25:01,967 --> 01:25:03,833
There is power enough to seize

2869
01:25:03,833 --> 01:25:06,033
or destroy the world!

2870
01:25:06,033 --> 01:25:10,133
And only I, I know how to
release and control it!

2871
01:25:11,600 --> 01:25:13,967
- [Joel] No brag, just fact.

2872
01:25:15,900 --> 01:25:17,333
- [Tom] Hey!

2873
01:25:17,333 --> 01:25:18,200
Shooters!

2874
01:25:18,200 --> 01:25:19,133
All right!

2875
01:25:19,133 --> 01:25:20,033
The source of all your power.

2876
01:25:20,033 --> 01:25:20,867
It's Cuervo!

2877
01:25:20,867 --> 01:25:22,133
Woo!

2878
01:25:22,133 --> 01:25:23,433
- [Crow] I'm gonna
need a lime, boss.

2879
01:25:23,433 --> 01:25:25,567
My gag reflexes is
right at the surface.

2880
01:25:25,567 --> 01:25:27,733
(Zorka mutters)

2881
01:25:27,733 --> 01:25:29,333
- Which would be
fatal to open it!

2882
01:25:29,333 --> 01:25:30,467
- [Joel] And you
could keep drink.

2883
01:25:30,467 --> 01:25:31,500
Make it ahead of time!

2884
01:25:31,500 --> 01:25:32,467
Keep it in the freezer!

2885
01:25:32,467 --> 01:25:33,733
Makes bump-ups, too!

2886
01:25:33,733 --> 01:25:35,033
- [Tom] It's a nice bouquet!

2887
01:25:35,033 --> 01:25:36,233
Good legs!

2888
01:25:36,233 --> 01:25:37,667
It's a real smoky
single malt! (slurps)

2889
01:25:37,667 --> 01:25:38,833
Slunge!

2890
01:25:38,833 --> 01:25:40,267
- [Joel] Finish it!

2891
01:25:40,267 --> 01:25:43,767
(upbeat electronic music)

2892
01:25:45,633 --> 01:25:47,233
- Bring her closer!

2893
01:25:48,700 --> 01:25:50,733
Reacts to her, definitely!

2894
01:25:50,733 --> 01:25:52,300
Or to something she's carrying!

2895
01:25:52,300 --> 01:25:53,967
- [Tom] Squeeze her gently.

2896
01:25:53,967 --> 01:25:55,833
- Oh, so it's just a hold-up!

2897
01:25:55,833 --> 01:25:57,367
- [Crow] I'll give
you five dollars

2898
01:25:57,367 --> 01:25:58,667
if you have a hard-boiled
egg in your purse!

2899
01:25:58,667 --> 01:25:59,500
- One of Zorka's disks!

2900
01:25:59,500 --> 01:26:00,433
Where'd you get it?

2901
01:26:00,433 --> 01:26:01,733
- At Doctor Zorka's house.

2902
01:26:01,733 --> 01:26:02,800
Under a withered plant.

2903
01:26:02,800 --> 01:26:04,000
- [Crow] His wife?

2904
01:26:04,000 --> 01:26:04,833
- Yes, I remember.
(Tom chuckles)

2905
01:26:04,833 --> 01:26:06,400
I meant to take it.

2906
01:26:06,400 --> 01:26:08,467
- That's the thing it reacts to!

2907
01:26:08,467 --> 01:26:10,100
- And that's the clue
for our antidote!

2908
01:26:10,100 --> 01:26:11,267
- [Joel] And that's
the thing that we,

2909
01:26:11,267 --> 01:26:12,533
hey wait!

2910
01:26:12,533 --> 01:26:13,667
- [Tom] Oh, hey, you
gettin' a good draw

2911
01:26:13,667 --> 01:26:15,267
off of that thing?

2912
01:26:16,333 --> 01:26:17,867
- [Crow] He's ours!

2913
01:26:17,867 --> 01:26:18,800
We're gonna have to brand him!

2914
01:26:18,800 --> 01:26:20,033
You hold him down, Hoss!

2915
01:26:20,033 --> 01:26:21,800
Little Joe, keep
those thing, get,

2916
01:26:21,800 --> 01:26:23,033
make it hot!
(men chatting)

2917
01:26:23,033 --> 01:26:25,700
- Getting stronger
with every beat!

2918
01:26:25,700 --> 01:26:29,300
(robots speaking in
foreign language)

2919
01:26:29,300 --> 01:26:31,600
- We're lucky last night
that we got one of you!

2920
01:26:31,600 --> 01:26:33,600
It's unfortunate the
G-Men are on this!

2921
01:26:33,600 --> 01:26:35,167
- Well, they are
in on it, Chief.

2922
01:26:35,167 --> 01:26:36,367
We gotta act quick

2923
01:26:36,367 --> 01:26:38,633
if we expect to beat
them to Zorka's secret!

2924
01:26:38,633 --> 01:26:39,767
Wherever it is.

2925
01:26:39,767 --> 01:26:41,467
- Do you think Monk's go it?

2926
01:26:41,467 --> 01:26:42,667
- [Tom] Oh, sure.

2927
01:26:42,667 --> 01:26:43,433
He wrote around
midnight, didn't he?

2928
01:26:43,433 --> 01:26:44,700
- Strange.

2929
01:26:44,700 --> 01:26:47,333
Almost as if he was
under a hypnotic spell.

2930
01:26:47,333 --> 01:26:48,267
- [Crow] You now,

2931
01:26:48,267 --> 01:26:49,700
I like this hypnotic spell bit!

2932
01:26:49,700 --> 01:26:51,033
- Perhaps he is!

2933
01:26:52,200 --> 01:26:53,667
Has it ever occurred to you

2934
01:26:53,667 --> 01:26:56,333
that Zorka might be alive?

2935
01:26:56,333 --> 01:26:57,533
- No, what do you mean?

2936
01:26:57,533 --> 01:26:58,800
- [Tom] I mean,
Zorka might be alive!

2937
01:26:58,800 --> 01:27:01,067
- He has done some
remarkable things.

2938
01:27:01,067 --> 01:27:03,267
He's never quite
right to me either.

2939
01:27:03,267 --> 01:27:05,400
That he should die in
an ordinary accident.

2940
01:27:05,400 --> 01:27:06,400
- [Joel] I'd always imagined him

2941
01:27:06,400 --> 01:27:08,233
doing something real splashy!

2942
01:27:08,233 --> 01:27:09,733
- Bring him to me!

2943
01:27:09,733 --> 01:27:11,700
Perhaps the sight of money
will loosen his tongue!

2944
01:27:11,700 --> 01:27:12,633
- [Tom] Hey!

2945
01:27:12,633 --> 01:27:13,867
- I know some other ways, too!

2946
01:27:13,867 --> 01:27:14,700
- [Crow] Like beating
him over the head

2947
01:27:14,700 --> 01:27:15,700
with hedge shears!

2948
01:27:15,700 --> 01:27:16,967
- Our leader is expecting us

2949
01:27:16,967 --> 01:27:18,800
to get control of
this great secret!

2950
01:27:18,800 --> 01:27:21,233
With it, we can
conquer the world!

2951
01:27:21,233 --> 01:27:23,700
- [Tom] Then we
start thinking big.

2952
01:27:23,700 --> 01:27:24,767
- [Joel] Mayberry!

2953
01:27:24,767 --> 01:27:26,233
My favorite town!

2954
01:27:26,233 --> 01:27:27,400
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

2955
01:27:34,900 --> 01:27:37,033
Here he goes!
(Joel squeaks)

2956
01:27:37,033 --> 01:27:37,933
String in the door.

2957
01:27:37,933 --> 01:27:39,167
I saw it.

2958
01:27:39,167 --> 01:27:40,533
Cheap.

2959
01:27:40,533 --> 01:27:42,000
- You passed out 'cause
you had the disks

2960
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:44,567
we'd planted on Ann Zorka.

2961
01:27:44,567 --> 01:27:46,167
- Who'd wanna destroy her?

2962
01:27:46,167 --> 01:27:47,000
- [Tom] Oh, I would!

2963
01:27:47,000 --> 01:27:49,100
- [Crow] Me too!

2964
01:27:49,100 --> 01:27:50,867
- Can I take this along
to Zorka's laboratory?

2965
01:27:50,867 --> 01:27:51,900
It might lead to something.

2966
01:27:51,900 --> 01:27:53,000
- Certainly!

2967
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:54,100
I'll assemble and analysis

2968
01:27:54,100 --> 01:27:55,300
of what is on that disk.

2969
01:27:55,300 --> 01:27:57,733
It might lead directly
to Zorka's secret!

2970
01:27:57,733 --> 01:27:58,867
- [Crow] Oh, don't get up!

2971
01:27:58,867 --> 01:27:59,700
- Come on.

2972
01:28:01,600 --> 01:28:02,667
- [Tom] Lazy.

2973
01:28:04,033 --> 01:28:06,367
- [Crow] There he doesn' go.

2974
01:28:06,367 --> 01:28:07,933
- [Tom] Oh-ho, fun!

2975
01:28:07,933 --> 01:28:10,700
- (mumbles) The Zorka disks.

2976
01:28:10,700 --> 01:28:11,967
- I hope you get get
enough other information

2977
01:28:11,967 --> 01:28:13,533
so that we can crack
this case wide open!

2978
01:28:13,533 --> 01:28:14,800
- Yeah, before it cracks us!

2979
01:28:14,800 --> 01:28:16,433
(Joel and robots laughing)

2980
01:28:16,433 --> 01:28:17,600
- [Tom] So, with grenadine,

2981
01:28:17,600 --> 01:28:18,433
or without, my dear?

2982
01:28:18,433 --> 01:28:19,833
(mixture bubbling)

2983
01:28:19,833 --> 01:28:22,533
- Now if I can just
get this formula

2984
01:28:22,533 --> 01:28:23,967
properly recorded--

2985
01:28:23,967 --> 01:28:27,733
- [Tom] I can get a
contract with Dave Getham!

2986
01:28:27,733 --> 01:28:29,200
Oh, wait a minute.

2987
01:28:29,200 --> 01:28:31,400
He casts a shadow?
(mixture bubbling)

2988
01:28:31,400 --> 01:28:32,900
- [Joel] Now, would you prefer

2989
01:28:32,900 --> 01:28:34,933
a Long Island Iced Tea?

2990
01:28:34,933 --> 01:28:37,700
- [Tom] Did he
have a hairnet on?

2991
01:28:37,700 --> 01:28:38,867
With casting.

2992
01:28:38,867 --> 01:28:40,000
(container clatters
and explodes)

2993
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:40,800
